<Doc titleZh="自托管：Cloudflare Workers 或 Docker" descriptionZh="在 Cloudflare Workers 加 Postgres 上运行 Montral，或用一个 Docker 容器部署。" description="Run Montral on Cloudflare Workers with Postgres, or in one Docker container." title="Self-host" updated="2026-11-10" toc>
  <div lang="en">
    <h1>Self-host Montral</h1>
    <p class="lede">Run your own copy on Cloudflare Workers or in Docker. Both use the same code and a Postgres database you control.</p>
    <p>Pick one:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#docker"><strong>Docker</strong></a>: one container plus Postgres, on any machine. Quickest to try.</li>
      <li><a href="#cloudflare"><strong>Cloudflare Workers</strong></a>: two Workers, a Queue and Hyperdrive in front of Postgres. Runs checks from Cloudflare's network.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="docker">Docker</h2>
    <p>One container runs the API, the web app and the check scheduler. The compose file also starts Postgres.</p>
    <h3>Requirements</h3>
    <ul><li>Docker with Compose v2</li><li>A machine that can reach the services you want to monitor</li></ul>
    <h3>Start it</h3>
    <p><strong>Private source build.</strong> No Montral container image or release has been published. Access to the private GitHub repository is required.</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>git clone https://github.com/TheHalfMoon/Montral.git
cd Montral
cp .env.docker.example .env
# Set POSTGRES_PASSWORD and BETTER_AUTH_SECRET in .env (openssl rand -hex 32)
docker compose up -d --build</code></pre>
    <p>Open <code>http://localhost:8080</code> and sign up. The schema is migrated automatically on every start and the data lives in the <code>pgdata</code> volume.</p>
    <h3>Put it on a domain</h3>
    <p>Run it behind a reverse proxy that terminates HTTPS (Caddy, nginx, Traefik, a load balancer) and set <code>PUBLIC_URL</code> in <code>.env</code> to the public address, for example <code>https://status.example.com</code>. Cookies, OAuth and links in emails all use this value, so sign-in will not work from a different origin than the one configured.</p>
    <h3>Settings (<code>.env</code>)</h3>
    <table class="vars">
      <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>POSTGRES_PASSWORD</code></td><td>Required. Password of the bundled Postgres.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code></td><td>Required. Signs sessions. Generate with <code>openssl rand -hex 32</code> and keep it stable.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>PUBLIC_URL</code></td><td>Public origin. Default <code>http://localhost:8080</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>PORT</code></td><td>Host port. Default <code>8080</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DISABLE_SIGNUP</code></td><td>Set to <code>true</code> to close registration once your own account exists. Invited people can still join.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>LEGAL_LINKS</code></td><td>Set to <code>true</code> to add "you agree to the Terms and Privacy Policy" to the sign-up form. The bundled <code>/terms</code> and <code>/privacy</code> pages describe the hosted service at montral.invalid: replace them with your own text first.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY</code><br /><code>TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY</code></td><td>Set both to put a <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/">Cloudflare Turnstile</a> check on the email sign-up form; the API verifies the token too. GitHub sign-in is not covered.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>INVITE_TTL_DAYS</code></td><td>How long invitations stay valid. Default 7.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS</code></td><td>How long workspace audit events are kept, 30 to 3650 days. Default 365.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CRON_SECRET</code></td><td>Optional. Lets an external scheduler call <code>POST /internal/run-checks</code>; unset leaves <code>/internal/*</code> closed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>MONTRAL_REPLAY_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code></td><td>Set to <code>true</code> to let webhook replay reach private development endpoints such as <code>localhost</code>. Separate from <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code> because replay shows the endpoint's response to the workspace manager; link-local and cloud metadata addresses stay refused. Leave it unset on instances other people sign up to.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code></td><td>Set to <code>true</code> to monitor internal services. By default monitors and alert webhooks pointing at private, loopback or link-local addresses (and single-label names such as compose service names) are refused, so a signed-up user cannot probe your network.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CHECK_USER_AGENT</code></td><td>Optional. User-Agent of HTTP checks.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>SELFCHECK_URLS</code></td><td>Optional. Comma-separated URLs a failed check fetches to tell a down target from an offline server. Unset uses three public sites; empty turns it off.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>PROBE_REGIONS</code><br><code>PROBE_SECRET</code></td><td>Optional. Remote probes for <a href="#regions">multi-region checks</a>. Unset, every check runs from this deployment.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>EMAIL_FROM</code><br>+ one transport</td><td>Optional outgoing email. Transport is <code>RESEND_API_KEY</code>, <code>SMTP_URL</code> (<code>smtps://user:pass@host:465</code>) or <code>SMTP_HOST</code> / <code>SMTP_PORT</code> / <code>SMTP_USER</code> / <code>SMTP_PASS</code> (<code>SMTP_SECURE=true</code> for port 465). Without it emails are written to the container log.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code><br><code>GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code></td><td>Optional "Sign in with GitHub". <a href="#github">Setup and troubleshooting</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN</code><br><code>PLAUSIBLE_SRC</code></td><td>Optional Plausible analytics. Off when the domain is empty.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>Operate</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Upgrade</strong>: pull the latest private source commit, then <code>docker compose up -d --build</code>. Migrations run on start. Back up first; see <a href="#upgrade">Upgrade and rollback</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>PostgreSQL version</strong>: <code>docker-compose.yml</code> pins <code>postgres:18.6-alpine</code> and its data directory. Never change the tag to another major version: PostgreSQL cannot read another major's data, and with the pinned directory an older or newer image refuses to start rather than creating a new, empty database. Move between majors with a dump and restore (<a href="/docs/backup">Backup and restore</a>).</li>
      <li><strong>Backup</strong>: <code>docker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U montral -Fc montral &gt; montral.dump</code>. Restore steps are in <a href="/docs/backup">Backup and restore</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Several containers</strong>: checks are leased with <code>FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED</code>, so more containers can share one database without duplicating checks.</li>
      <li><strong>Logs</strong>: <code>docker compose logs -f montral</code>. A health endpoint is at <code>/health</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Audit log retention</strong>: workspace audit events (Workspace, Audit log in the dashboard) are kept for <code>AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS</code> (default 365, at least 30) and pruned once an hour by the scheduler, on Docker and Workers alike. The <code>audit_event</code> table is append-only: a database trigger refuses UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE, except deletes made by the <code>montral_prune_audit</code> retention function and the cascade when a workspace is deleted. It protects against application mistakes, not against the database owner, who can still drop the trigger. Backups include the table like any other.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 id="upgrade">Upgrade and rollback</h3>
    <p>Migrations only go forward. Every step below is qualified in CI (<code>montral-upgrade.yml</code>): an installation of the previous release candidate, seeded with users, projects, monitors, channels, incidents, status pages, webhook inboxes, maintenance windows and API keys, is upgraded, rolled back and recovered from backups.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Back up first</strong>, with the app running: <code>docker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U montral -Fc montral &gt; montral-pre-upgrade.dump</code>, then <code>pg_restore --list montral-pre-upgrade.dump | head</code> to check the file. Keep it until you are sure you will not roll back.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade</strong>: update the source, then <code>docker compose up -d --build</code>. Migrations run in one transaction when the new container starts, before it accepts requests; containers starting together wait for each other. Data, sign-in sessions, API keys, share links, password pages, custom domains and webhook receiver URLs keep working (with the same <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>Check</strong>: <code>/health</code> answers, you can sign in, and monitors show new checks within a minute.</li>
    </ol>
    <p><strong>An older build does not start on an upgraded database</strong>, and it changes nothing. Builds from this version on exit at once with <code>database schema is newer than this Montral build; restore the pre-upgrade backup or run the newer build</code>. Earlier builds (up to the 17f55c1 release candidate) retry for about a minute, exit with the generic <code>Database connection/migration unavailable after bounded startup retries</code>, and the container keeps restarting. With any build, <code>pnpm --filter @montral/db-pg exec node migrate-plain.mjs --check</code> names the reason: <code>Database migration history is ahead of this build</code>. Going back to the old build therefore always means going back to the pre-upgrade backup:</p>
    <pre><code>docker compose stop montral
docker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U montral -Fc montral &gt; montral-upgraded.dump   # what the upgraded version wrote
docker compose exec postgres dropdb -U montral montral
docker compose exec postgres createdb -U montral montral
docker compose exec -T postgres pg_restore -U montral -d montral --no-owner &lt; montral-pre-upgrade.dump
# check out the previous source, then
docker compose up -d --build</code></pre>
    <ul>
      <li>Restore into an <strong>empty</strong> database as above. Do not restore a pre-upgrade backup over the upgraded database with <code>--clean</code>: tables and columns the upgrade added are not in the backup, so they would stay behind and a later upgrade could fail on them.</li>
      <li>Everything written after the upgrade (checks, incidents, settings) is not in the pre-upgrade backup; the extra dump keeps it in case you upgrade again.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Disaster recovery</strong> uses the same commands: restore the latest backup into a new, empty database (<a href="/docs/backup#restore">Backup and restore</a>), keep the same <code>.env</code>, and start the app; migrations newer than the backup run on start. For the synthetic installation in CI, from a dropped database to a verified, serving app (create database, restore, start, sign in and read everything back) took about 2 seconds; your time grows with the size of the database, mostly in <code>pg_restore</code>.</p>
    <h3 id="replicas">Several replicas behind a load balancer</h3>
    <p>For more capacity or to restart without downtime, run several app replicas on the same PostgreSQL behind one load balancer:</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>REPLICAS=2 docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.replicas.yml up -d --build</code></pre>
    <p>The replicas need no coordination of their own: scheduled checks, escalations, alert deliveries and maintenance are claimed in PostgreSQL, so each runs once in total, not once per replica; sessions live in PostgreSQL, so a sign-in works on every replica. The overlay puts nginx (<code>docker/lb-nginx.conf</code>) in front, re-reads Docker's DNS so restarted replicas are picked up, retries a refused connection on another replica, and sets <code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code> because it is the one proxy in front. Restart replicas one at a time (<code>docker restart</code> on each container, waiting until it is healthy) for an upgrade without dropped requests. Put TLS in front of the balancer (or terminate it there) for a public address, and size <code>DB_POOL_MAX</code> × replicas below PostgreSQL's <code>max_connections</code>. CI qualifies two replicas on every change: requests spread over both with one session, 60 concurrent webhooks stored once each, a rolling restart with no failed request, every 60-second check run 3–8 times in 330 seconds with no run claimed twice, and a failing monitor opening exactly one incident. Not qualified: replicas on different hosts, and a highly available PostgreSQL.</p>
    <h3 id="ping">Ping (ICMP) monitors</h3>
    <p>Ping monitors run the system <code>ping</code> binary of the server, so they work only on the self-hosted Node server (Docker or <code>node server.mjs</code>); a Cloudflare Workers deployment refuses to create them. The image is based on <code>node:22-alpine</code> and runs as the unprivileged <code>node</code> user, so it uses BusyBox <code>ping</code> with unprivileged ICMP sockets. Linux allows those for the groups listed in <code>net.ipv4.ping_group_range</code>; Docker 20.10 and later set it to <code>0 2147483647</code> in every container, so nothing needs to be configured. On an older engine, another runtime, or when the host's default is restricted, add this to the <code>montral</code> service in <code>docker-compose.yml</code>:</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>    sysctls:
      net.ipv4.ping_group_range: "0 2147483647"</code></pre>
    <p>The setting is per network namespace and does not affect the host. It cannot be used with <code>network_mode: host</code>; set it on the host instead. When <code>ping</code> is missing or may not send ICMP, checks are inconclusive with “Ping unavailable on this server” (the server's problem, not the target's): no alert is sent, and the server log says so once. Each check resolves the hostname once, refuses private and internal addresses unless <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code> is set (as for TCP monitors), and pings the validated IP address, preferring IPv4. IPv6 targets need IPv6 connectivity in the container (Docker networks are IPv4-only unless IPv6 is enabled); without it the check is reported as inconclusive. Outside Docker, the Linux <code>ping</code> from iputils normally has the <code>cap_net_raw</code> capability or relies on the same sysctl; macOS and Windows <code>ping</code> work without extra setup.</p>

    <h3 id="browser-checks">Browser checks (multi-step journeys)</h3>
    <p>Browser monitors run a journey of fixed steps (open a page, fill in a form, click, wait, check text, URL or status) in headless Chromium. They are off by default. In Docker they run in a separate <strong>browser-runner</strong> service, never in the app's container:</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>echo "BROWSER_RUNNER_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> .env
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.browser.yml up -d --build</code></pre>
    <p>The app keeps the default image (no browser). The override adds the <code>browser-runner</code> service, built from the Dockerfile's <code>browser-runner</code> target (Debian slim with the Chromium headless shell of the pinned Playwright version, about 1.2 GB; Playwright does not support Alpine), and turns browser checks on in the app with <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_URL</code>.</p>
    <p><strong>Why a separate service.</strong> A monitored page is code from the internet running in Chromium. If it ever escaped Chromium's sandbox inside the app's container, it could read the server's environment (database URL, auth secret). The runner is built so that such an escape finds nothing worth having:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>It receives no <code>DATABASE_URL</code>, no <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> and no other app setting: only <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_TOKEN</code> and its limits.</li>
      <li>It is on an internal network shared with the app only (no route out) and on its own egress network to the internet. It is not on the database's network, so PostgreSQL is neither resolvable nor routable from it.</li>
      <li>It accepts only jobs signed with <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_TOKEN</code>: HMAC-SHA256 over the method, path, timestamp, a random nonce and the body. Requests older than 60 seconds or replayed are refused with the same answer whatever the reason, bodies are capped at 512 KB, and every answer is signed back. A job carries one run's journey and only the secrets that run needs; those secrets are encrypted with a key derived from the token, while the rest of the job is signed but not encrypted, which is why the jobs network must stay internal. The app checks every answer against a strict schema and stores only fixed messages.</li>
      <li>It runs with Docker's init as PID 1 (<code>init: true</code>, which reaps orphaned processes) as an unprivileged user with <code>cap_drop: [ALL]</code>, <code>no-new-privileges</code>, a read-only root file system, size-limited <code>/tmp</code> and <code>/dev/shm</code>, and limits on processes (1024), memory (2 GB) and CPU (2).</li>
      <li>Its seccomp profile is Docker's default plus exactly <code>clone</code>, <code>unshare</code>, <code>setns</code> and <code>chroot</code> (<code>docker/browser-runner-seccomp.json</code>). These are what Chromium's own sandbox needs for its user, PID and network namespaces. Everything else Docker refuses stays refused.</li>
      <li>For even stronger isolation, run the runner under gVisor: add <code>runtime: runsc</code> to the service where gVisor is installed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Inside the runner, each check still gets its own short-lived worker process with its own temporary directory (deleted afterwards), and its own fresh Chromium with an empty profile, so cookies, storage and cache never pass from one check or workspace to the next. Chromium's only way out is a proxy inside that worker. It resolves each host once and connects only to the address it validated, which rules out DNS rebinding. Private and internal addresses are refused unless <code>BROWSER_CHECK_ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS=true</code>; <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code> does not open them to browsers. Loopback, link-local, cloud metadata, <code>localhost</code>, the runner's own addresses and the app's address are always refused. Non-proxied WebRTC traffic and QUIC are off. Journeys cannot run JavaScript of their own.</p>
    <p><strong>Without Docker</strong> (<code>node server.mjs</code>), browser checks can also run inside the app's process tree: install the pinned Chromium (<code>pnpm --filter @montral/e2e exec playwright install --with-deps chromium</code>, or set <code>BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH</code>), build the worker next to the server (<code>pnpm --filter @montral/api build:browser-worker</code>) and set <code>BROWSER_CHECKS=enabled</code>. Then Chromium runs as the same user as the server, and a sandbox escape could read its secrets. Prefer the runner: start <code>node browser-runner.mjs</code> (built with <code>pnpm --filter @montral/api build:browser-runner</code>) as a different user, without the app's environment, and set <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_URL</code> and <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_TOKEN</code> on the app. Chromium's sandbox cannot be turned off in production: <code>BROWSER_CHECK_SANDBOX=off</code> is accepted only when <code>NODE_ENV</code> is <code>development</code>, and otherwise makes browser checks unavailable. Creating a browser monitor is refused until the runner (or this server) has actually started Chromium once; the result is cached for ten minutes.</p>
    <p><strong>Fairness, limits and sizing.</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Browser monitors check at most every 5 minutes; faster intervals are raised.</li>
      <li><code>MAX_BROWSER_CHECKS</code> (default 2, up to 16) browser checks run at once, and at most one per workspace, so one tenant cannot take every slot. A few more checks wait up to 15 seconds for a slot. Beyond that a check is deferred. A workspace's browser monitors that are due together run one after another, in one queue task that spends at most 2 minutes on them (a check starts only while its worst case still fits; the rest are deferred), and one workspace never holds more than one queue slot for browser checks. A browser check's credit is taken just before its journey starts; a workspace without credits starts none (nothing is recorded, as for other monitors). A deferred check is retried within about a minute and its credit is given back; it shows on the monitor as at most one deferred run per interval, so retries never push real runs out of the history. Checks the runtime could not run (runner unreachable or refusing, Chromium not starting) are recorded as error runs and their credit is given back too. A monitor is shown as <em>unchecked</em> after 3 runtime errors in a row, or when its deferrals have lasted 3 of its intervals (counted from when the streak began, whatever the interval); the workspace's owners and admins then get one digest e-mail listing all unchecked browser monitors, at most one an hour per workspace (also in the alert log, one entry per project naming only that project's monitors). The next real run clears it, and so does pausing, resuming or changing what the monitor checks (interval, journey, target). The monitor page shows the browser runtime's state and its latest problem.</li>
      <li>Plan on about 600 MB of memory (measured: a simple journey peaks at 609 MiB for the whole process tree) and up to one CPU core per concurrent check: 2 GB and 2 cores, as set on the runner, for the default of 2.</li>
      <li><code>BROWSER_CHECK_MAX_RSS_MB</code> (default 1024) caps the memory of one check's whole process tree (worker, Chromium and its children), sampled every 250 ms on Linux; past it the tree is killed and the check fails with "Browser check exceeded its memory limit". Each check is also limited to 30 seconds of CPU time and to its journey timeout (at most 60 seconds) plus start-up and shutdown allowances. Page JavaScript has a 256 MB heap. A worker that crashes cannot leave Chromium behind: every process whose command line names the check's profile directory is killed with it.</li>
      <li>Each page may transfer at most 10 MB per connection and 25 MB per check, over at most 256 connections.</li>
      <li>Runs are kept per monitor: the latest 50, and screenshots (only when the monitor asks for them, on failure, at most 200 KB, with secret and password fields masked) on the latest 5 of those. Nothing older than 14 days is kept. Screenshots of runs that used secrets are shown to owners and admins only, decided per run; changing a monitor's secrets deletes them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Browser monitor secrets are encrypted with a key derived from <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> and bound to their workspace, monitor and name. Changing <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> makes them unreadable: the affected steps fail with "secret is not set" until the secrets are entered again. Browser checks do not run on Cloudflare Workers. On Windows and macOS the memory and CPU limits are not measured (time limits still apply); run them on Linux in production.</p>

    <h2 id="cloudflare">Cloudflare Workers</h2>
    <p>Two Workers: <code>montral-api</code> (the API under <code>/api/*</code>, the minute cron and the queue consumer) and <code>montral-web</code> (the site, which reaches the API through a service binding).</p>
    <h3>Requirements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A Cloudflare account and a domain on Cloudflare. The <strong>Workers Paid</strong> plan is needed only for the Queue mode below; the Free plan works in inline mode at small scale</li>
      <li>A Postgres database reachable from Cloudflare. It is accessed through Hyperdrive, so any hosted Postgres works (Neon, Supabase, RDS, your own)</li>
      <li>Node.js 22+ and pnpm (<code>corepack enable</code> gives you the pinned version). Wrangler is installed with the project; sign in with <code>pnpm exec wrangler login</code> in <code>apps/api</code></li>
    </ul>
    <h3>1. Get the code</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>git clone https://github.com/TheHalfMoon/Montral.git
cd montral
pnpm install</code></pre>
    <h3>2. Choose how checks run, then create Hyperdrive</h3>
    <p>Checks run in one of two modes. The mode follows from whether the <code>queues</code> block exists in <code>apps/api/wrangler.jsonc</code>, so it is a config switch, not a code change.</p>
    <table class="vars">
      <thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Plan</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Queue</strong> (default)</td><td>Workers <strong>Paid</strong></td><td>The cron fans due monitors out to a Queue, 25 per message, and the consumer runs them in parallel invocations. Scales to thousands of monitors.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Inline</strong></td><td>Free or Paid</td><td>No Queue. The minute cron runs the checks itself, up to <strong>40 monitors per minute</strong>, within the Free plan's 50-subrequest and 10 ms CPU limits. Small installs only.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><strong>Queue mode</strong> (the file ships this way): create the queue once.</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>pnpm exec wrangler queues create montral-checks</code></pre>
    <p><strong>Inline mode</strong>: delete the whole <code>"queues"</code> block from <code>apps/api/wrangler.jsonc</code> and skip the command above. Without a bound queue the Worker detects it and runs checks inline.</p>
    <p>Then create Hyperdrive and copy its id into the <code>hyperdrive</code> block of <code>apps/api/wrangler.jsonc</code>:</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>pnpm exec wrangler hyperdrive create montral-prod --connection-string="postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db"</code></pre>
    <h3>3. Create the schema</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db" pnpm db:migrate</code></pre>
    <p>It never issues <code>CREATE SCHEMA</code>, so a database role without database-level <code>CREATE</code> works too. Run it again after every upgrade.</p>
    <p>Before an upgrade you can check the database without changing it: <code>DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db" pnpm --filter @montral/db-pg exec node migrate-plain.mjs --check</code> verifies the applied history matches this version and lists the migrations that would run. Migrations run in one transaction, so <code>CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY</code> is not supported, and an enum value added in one migration cannot be used by a later migration in the same run.</p>
    <h3>4. Point the config at your domain</h3>
    <p>In <code>apps/api/wrangler.jsonc</code> set <code>routes</code> (<code>your-domain/api/*</code>), <code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code> and <code>WEB_ORIGIN</code> (both <code>https://your-domain</code>) and <code>EMAIL_FROM</code>. Remove the <code>placement</code> block, or set it to your own database host.</p>
    <p>In <code>apps/web/wrangler.jsonc</code> set the custom-domain <code>routes</code> pattern and <code>PRODUCT_URL</code> (where "Powered by" links to; use your own origin).</p>
    <h3>5. Secrets</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>cd apps/api
pnpm exec wrangler secret put BETTER_AUTH_SECRET     # openssl rand -hex 32
pnpm exec wrangler secret put CRON_SECRET            # any long random string; guards /internal/*
# optional "Sign in with GitHub": wrangler secret put GITHUB_CLIENT_ID, then GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET (see the GitHub sign-in section)</code></pre>
    <h3>6. Deploy</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>cd apps/api &amp;&amp; pnpm exec wrangler deploy
cd ../web &amp;&amp; pnpm build &amp;&amp; pnpm exec wrangler deploy</code></pre>
    <p>Deploy the API first: the web Worker binds to it. Then open your domain and sign up.</p>
    <h3>Settings</h3>
    <table class="vars vars-3">
      <thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>Variable</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code><br><code>WEB_ORIGIN</code></td><td>Public origin of the site. Used for cookies, OAuth and email links.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>EMAIL_FROM</code></td><td>Sender address. Onboard the domain in Cloudflare Email Sending; without it emails are logged.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>INVITE_TTL_DAYS</code></td><td>How long invitations stay valid. Default 7.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS</code></td><td>How long workspace audit events are kept, 30 to 3650 days. Default 365.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code></td><td>Set to <code>true</code> to let monitors and alert webhooks target private addresses. Default: refused. Cloudflare Workers cannot reach private ranges anyway; this mostly matters for Docker.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars + secret</td><td><code>PROBE_REGIONS</code>, <code>PROBE_SECRET</code></td><td>Optional. Remote probes for <a href="#regions">multi-region checks</a>. Put the region list in <code>vars</code> and the shared secret with <code>wrangler secret put PROBE_SECRET</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>DISABLE_SIGNUP</code></td><td>Set to <code>true</code> to close registration (email and GitHub). Create your own account first; afterwards only people with a pending invitation can still sign up.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>LEGAL_LINKS</code></td><td>Set to <code>true</code> to add "you agree to the Terms and Privacy Policy" to the sign-up form. The bundled <code>/terms</code> and <code>/privacy</code> pages describe the hosted service at montral.invalid: replace them with your own text first.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars + secret</td><td><code>TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY</code>, <code>TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY</code></td><td>Optional. Put the site key in the API <code>vars</code> and the secret key with <code>wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY</code>; email sign-up then requires a verified Turnstile token. Both must be set.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api secrets</td><td><code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code><br><code>CRON_SECRET</code></td><td>See step 5.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>web vars</td><td><code>PRODUCT_URL</code></td><td>Target of the "Powered by" link on status pages.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>web vars</td><td><code>PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN</code><br><code>PLAUSIBLE_SRC</code></td><td>Optional analytics. Off when the domain is unset.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>How checks run</h3>
    <p>A cron trigger fires every minute and leases the monitors that are due. In Queue mode it packs them 25 per message into the <code>montral-checks</code> Queue, and the queue consumer runs each pack, records results, opens and resolves incidents and sends alerts. In inline mode the cron does all of that itself for up to 40 monitors per run.</p>
    <h3>Upgrade</h3>
    <p>Pull the new code, run the migration again (it only applies what is new), then deploy the API and the web Worker in that order.</p>
    <h3>Switching modes later</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Free to Paid</strong>: upgrade the plan, restore the <code>queues</code> block, run <code>pnpm exec wrangler queues create montral-checks</code>, then <code>pnpm exec wrangler deploy</code> the API.</li>
      <li><strong>Paid to Free</strong>: remove the <code>queues</code> block and deploy the API again. You can delete the queue afterwards.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No data migration is involved. Monitors, history and incidents are untouched.</p>

    <h2 id="regions">Multi-region checks</h2>
    <p>By default a monitor is checked from where Montral runs. To check from several places, deploy the small probe in <code>apps/probe</code> to a few regions and tell the API where they are. A monitor uses them only when you pick regions for it; everything else keeps running from this deployment, so nothing changes until you opt in. How a verdict is reached and what the app shows are covered in <a href="/docs/regions">Multi-region checks</a>.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Deploy the probe</strong> in each place you want checks to come from. It is a small service that runs one check on request, and there are two ways to run it. Pick whichever fits, or mix them: every probe is just a URL to the API.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>Option A: Docker or any Node host</h3>
    <p>The probe is a plain Node server, so it runs on any VPS or machine in any country. The image is built from the repository root:</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>docker build -f apps/probe/Dockerfile -t montral-probe .
docker run -d --restart unless-stopped -p 8787:8787 \
  -e PROBE_SECRET=&lt;a long random string&gt; -e PROBE_REGION=sao-paulo \
  montral-probe</code></pre>
    <p><code>apps/probe/docker-compose.yml</code> wraps it (builds from this private repository; no public probe image exists) and can add HTTPS with Caddy: <code is:raw>PROBE_DOMAIN=probe-sao.example.com docker compose --profile tls up -d</code>. Without Docker, run <code>pnpm --filter @montral/probe build:node</code> and then <code>PROBE_SECRET=… node apps/probe/dist/server.mjs</code> (Node 22). The API needs an <code>https</code> URL, so put the probe behind a reverse proxy or the bundled Caddy. Docker and Node probes answer <code>GET /</code> with <code is:raw>{"ok":true,"region":"…"}</code> for health checks; on Vercel the same answer is at <code>/api/probe/&lt;id&gt;</code> and the root path is a 404.</p>
    <p>Settings: <code>PROBE_SECRET</code> (required), <code>PROBE_REGION</code> (a label), <code>PORT</code> (default 8787), <code>HOST</code> (default 0.0.0.0), <code>CHECK_USER_AGENT</code> (same as on the API). Private and internal targets are refused unless you set <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS=true</code> on that probe, which is what lets a probe inside your office or home network check internal services. Only do it for a probe that lives in the network you want to watch.</p>
    <h3>Option B: Vercel, several regions at once</h3>
    <p>The bundled build creates one function per region (<code>apps/probe/regions.json</code>, default: Virginia, San Francisco, Frankfurt, Singapore, Tokyo). Set <code>PROBE_SECRET</code> on the Vercel project, run <code>pnpm build:vercel</code> in <code>apps/probe</code>, then <code>vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod</code>. Running a function in several regions needs a Vercel plan that allows it.</p>
    <ol start="2">
      <li><strong>Tell the API.</strong> Set the same secret as <code>PROBE_SECRET</code> and list the regions as JSON in <code>PROBE_REGIONS</code>:</li>
    </ol>
    <pre><code is:raw>PROBE_SECRET=&lt;the same secret as on the probe&gt;
PROBE_REGIONS={"us-east":"https://probe.example.app/api/probe/us-east","eu-central":"https://probe.example.app/api/probe/eu-central","ap-southeast":{"url":"https://probe.example.app/api/probe/ap-southeast","name":"Singapore"}}</code></pre>
    <p>Keys are region ids you choose (lowercase letters, digits and dashes). A value is a URL, or <code is:raw>{ "url", "name" }</code> to set the label shown in the app. URLs must be <code>https</code> (plain <code>http</code> is accepted for <code>localhost</code> only). The list appears in the app and in <code>GET /api/regions</code>, and a monitor can then pick up to its plan's limit.</p>
    <h3>How it behaves</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Only <strong>HTTP, TCP and WebSocket</strong> monitors can use regions. Other types, and heartbeats, always run from this deployment.</li>
      <li>With several regions a run counts as failed only when <strong>most of the regions that answered</strong> failed, so one region's bad route does not open an incident. Each region's result is kept, and the monitor page shows uptime and latency per region.</li>
      <li>A probe that cannot be reached is not a failed check. It is left out of the vote, and when no probe answers the check runs from this deployment instead, so a probe outage cannot blind monitoring.</li>
      <li>Each region counts as one check against any check allowance. A single request can also be sent from one region on the monitor page (or <code>POST /api/monitors/:id/check</code> with a <code>region</code>); it is not recorded and does not change the monitor's status.</li>
      <li>Probes only accept signed requests (HMAC-SHA256 over timestamp and body, 60 s skew) and refuse private, loopback and link-local targets whatever the signature (unless its own operator turns <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code> on), so a probe cannot be used as an open proxy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="github">GitHub sign-in</h2>
    <p>"Continue with GitHub" is optional and off until you configure a GitHub OAuth App. Without it the GitHub button is hidden everywhere (web and mobile app) and email sign-in keeps working unchanged.</p>
    <h3>1. Create the OAuth App</h3>
    <p>In GitHub, open <strong>Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps → New OAuth App</strong> (or the same page of an organization). Fill in:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Homepage URL</strong>: your public address, for example <code>https://status.example.com</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Authorization callback URL</strong>: <code>&lt;BETTER_AUTH_URL&gt;/api/auth/callback/github</code>, exactly. With Docker <code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code> is your <code>PUBLIC_URL</code>; on Cloudflare it is the <code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code> var of the API Worker, the public origin of the site (the API is served at <code>/api</code> on the same domain). Example: <code>https://status.example.com/api/auth/callback/github</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Create a client secret and keep both values.</p>
    <h3>2. Set the two variables</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Docker</strong>: add <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code> to <code>.env</code>, then <code>docker compose up -d</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: in <code>apps/api</code> run <code>pnpm exec wrangler secret put GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>pnpm exec wrangler secret put GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code>, then redeploy the API Worker.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>3. Check it</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>curl https://status.example.com/api/config
# "auth": { ..., "github": true, ... }</code></pre>
    <p>Both variables must be set; with only one, <code>github</code> stays <code>false</code>. Signed-in users can then connect or disconnect GitHub under <strong>Account → Connected accounts</strong>, even when the GitHub email differs from the account email. A GitHub login is only matched to an existing account by email when GitHub reports that address as verified, and an account always keeps at least one way to sign in. <code>DISABLE_SIGNUP</code> also applies to first-time GitHub sign-ins.</p>
    <p>A first GitHub sign-in creates the account and its personal workspace; it has no password. To add one, use <em>Forgot password</em> with the GitHub email (this needs outgoing email to be configured). Deleting such an account needs a recent sign-in instead of a password.</p>
    <p>The mobile app uses the same provider: it reads <code>auth.github</code> from <code>/api/config</code> and opens the same OAuth App through <code>/api/auth/native/github</code>, so there is nothing extra to register (see <a href="/docs/api#native-signin">native sign-in</a>).</p>
    <h3>Troubleshooting</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>"redirect_uri is not associated with this application"</strong>: the callback URL in the OAuth App differs from <code>&lt;BETTER_AUTH_URL&gt;/api/auth/callback/github</code> (scheme, host, port or path). Fix it in GitHub, not in the app.</li>
      <li><strong>The callback goes to the wrong host</strong>: <code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code> (<code>PUBLIC_URL</code> in Docker) is wrong, often still <code>localhost</code>. Set it to the public address and restart.</li>
      <li><strong>Behind a proxy</strong>: terminate HTTPS at the proxy and pass the original <code>Host</code> and <code>X-Forwarded-Proto</code> headers. The public address configured above is what GitHub must be given.</li>
      <li><strong>Button missing</strong>: <code>/api/config</code> shows <code>github: false</code>, so a variable is empty or the service was not restarted.</li>
      <li><strong>"Sign-ups are closed"</strong>: <code>DISABLE_SIGNUP=true</code>; invite the person first, or connect GitHub from an existing account.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="sso">Single sign-on (OpenID Connect)</h2>
    <p>Montral can sign people in through any OpenID Connect identity provider. There are two ways to set it up, and both can be used at once:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Per workspace</strong> (no server configuration): the workspace owner adds a connection under <strong>Settings → Single sign-on</strong>. People whose email is in one of the workspace's <em>verified</em> domains get an account in that workspace on their first sign-in.</li>
      <li><strong>Instance-wide</strong>: the operator sets <code>OIDC_ISSUER</code>, <code>OIDC_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET</code> (optionally <code>OIDC_ALLOWED_DOMAINS</code>). First sign-ins then create an ordinary account with its own personal workspace, like a sign-up, and <code>DISABLE_SIGNUP</code> applies.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>1. Register Montral at the identity provider</h3>
    <p>Create an OpenID Connect (OAuth 2.0) <em>web application</em> / confidential client with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Redirect URI</strong>: <code>&lt;BETTER_AUTH_URL&gt;/api/auth/sso/callback</code>, exactly (with Docker that is <code>&lt;PUBLIC_URL&gt;/api/auth/sso/callback</code>). The settings page shows it. Montral never accepts another redirect target.</li>
      <li><strong>Grant</strong>: authorization code, with PKCE (S256). <strong>Scopes</strong>: <code>openid email profile</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Client authentication</strong>: client secret (HTTP Basic or POST body).</li>
      <li><strong>id_token signing</strong>: an asymmetric algorithm (RS256, PS256, ES256, EdDSA…). HMAC (HS256) and <code>none</code> are refused.</li>
      <li>The id_token must carry <code>email</code> and <code>email_verified: true</code> (the boolean). Sign-ins without it are refused, and there is deliberately no setting to trust an email without it: an unverified address would let an identity provider claim any account.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>2. Configure the connection</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Issuer URL</strong>: the provider's issuer, exactly as its <code>/.well-known/openid-configuration</code> names it (Montral checks that it matches, character for character). Use <strong>Test connection</strong> to check it.</li>
      <li><strong>Client ID</strong> and <strong>client secret</strong>. The secret is stored encrypted (AES-256-GCM, with a key derived from <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code>) and is never shown again, returned by the API or written to the audit log. Changing <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> makes stored secrets unreadable: enter them again afterwards. Changing the issuer or the client ID requires entering the secret again, and the secret is only ever sent to the token endpoint the provider named when it was entered: if discovery later names another one, sign-ins stop (<code>connection_misconfigured</code>) until the owner saves the secret again.</li>
      <li><strong>Email domains</strong>, then publish the TXT record shown for each (<code>_montral-challenge.&lt;domain&gt;</code>) and press <strong>Verify</strong>. Only verified domains sign anyone in, and a domain can be verified by one workspace per instance. Keep the record: it is looked up again about every 6 hours (every 30 minutes while failing), and verification is withdrawn when the record has been missing or wrong for 24 hours (or DNS unreachable for 7 days). A withdrawn domain signs nobody in and can then be verified by another workspace that publishes its own record.</li>
      <li><strong>Role for new people</strong>: member (default) or admin. Never owner.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Example settings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Keycloak</strong>: issuer <code>https://keycloak.example.com/realms/&lt;realm&gt;</code>. Create a client with <em>Client authentication</em> and <em>Standard flow</em> on, set <em>Valid redirect URIs</em> to the redirect URI, and keep <em>Email verified</em> set on users.</li>
      <li><strong>Authentik</strong>: issuer <code>https://authentik.example.com/application/o/&lt;application-slug&gt;/</code> (with the trailing slash). Create an OAuth2/OpenID provider (confidential, with a signing key so tokens are RS256) and an application. Authentik's default email mapping may report <code>email_verified: false</code>; map it to true only for addresses Authentik really verified.</li>
      <li><strong>Microsoft Entra ID</strong>: issuer <code>https://login.microsoftonline.com/&lt;tenant-id&gt;/v2.0</code> (one tenant; the multi-tenant <code>common</code> endpoint has no fixed issuer and is not supported). Register a <em>Web</em> application with the redirect URI and a client secret, and add the optional <code>email</code> claim. Entra ID does not send <code>email_verified</code> by default, so sign-ins are refused until it does: add it with a claims-mapping policy that emits <code>true</code> only for addresses in domains verified in your tenant, or put Keycloak or Authentik in front of Entra ID as a broker that asserts it.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Workspace</strong>: issuer <code>https://accounts.google.com</code>. Create an OAuth client ID of type <em>Web application</em> in Google Cloud with the redirect URI, and verify your Workspace domain in Montral. Any Google account can reach the consent screen, so only the verified domains decide who gets in.</li>
      <li><strong>Okta</strong>: issuer <code>https://&lt;your-org&gt;.okta.com</code> (or a custom authorization server such as <code>https://&lt;your-org&gt;.okta.com/oauth2/default</code>). Create an OIDC <em>Web Application</em> with the authorization code grant and the redirect URI.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Existing accounts</h3>
    <p>A person who already has a Montral account with the same email is <strong>not</strong> signed in or linked automatically, even when the domain is verified: an identity provider (or a workspace owner who controls one) could otherwise take over any account with a matching address. They see "An account with this email already exists" and link once: sign in as usual (password, two-step verification or GitHub), open <strong>Account → Single sign-on</strong> and choose <strong>Link single sign-on</strong>. The provider must confirm the account's own email address. After that, SSO signs them in. Linking is a way to sign in, not a membership: someone who is not yet a member of the workspace still needs an invitation. People with no Montral account are created on their first sign-in (just in time), with a verified email and no password, as members of the connection's workspace. Removing someone from the workspace signs them out, removes their SSO link to it and remembers the removal (their address and SSO identities), so SSO never signs them back in, re-adds them or, even after they delete their account, provisions them again; to return they need to accept a new invitation to their address (a pending or cancelled invitation does not lift the block).</p>
    <p>For the same reason a social sign-in (GitHub) never links itself to an account that has an SSO identity, or that belongs to a workspace requiring SSO, because the email matches: connect it from <strong>Account → Connected accounts</strong> while signed in.</p>
    <h3>Require single sign-on</h3>
    <p>With <strong>Require single sign-on</strong> on, every member of the workspace except the owner can only use the workspace through this connection: password, GitHub and other sign-ins (including the operator's instance-wide provider) are refused for them; when the switch is turned on their other sessions are signed out, and any session not created by this connection gets <code>403</code> on the workspace, also for the actions Better Auth runs itself (invitations, roles, the active workspace, agent consent, API keys). The <strong>owner is the break-glass account</strong>: they keep password sign-in, so a provider outage or misconfiguration cannot lock the workspace out. Protect that account with a strong password and two-step verification. Requiring SSO needs at least one verified domain, and switching the connection off lifts the requirement. Their API keys only work on the workspace when they were created from a session this connection signed in, and an agent (OAuth) token only while the SSO session that authorized it is still signed in; others are refused with <code>403</code> (keys work again if the requirement is lifted). Authorizing an agent, or exporting one's account, needs such a session for every require-SSO workspace the person belongs to (so someone in two require-SSO workspaces with different providers cannot do either). Someone who accepts an invitation while signed in another way becomes a member, but can do nothing in the workspace (it is also left out of their workspace list, and its members-only status pages stay hidden) until they sign in with SSO. Changing the connection's issuer or client signs out the sessions it created. The owner's own sessions, keys and agents are not bound to SSO.</p>
    <p><strong>Offboarding:</strong> there is no SCIM, so removing someone at the identity provider only stops new SSO sign-ins. Remove them from the workspace too (this signs them out and blocks re-provisioning) and revoke the API keys and agent authorizations they made: an API key made from an SSO session keeps working until it is revoked.</p>
    <h3>Security notes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Authorization code flow with PKCE (S256), a single-use <code>state</code> stored only as a hash and bound to the browser that started the sign-in (a cookie), a <code>nonce</code>, a 10-minute limit, and the redirect URI fixed to this server's address.</li>
      <li>id_tokens are verified with the provider's JWKS (refetched on an unknown key id, for key rotation, at most every 30 seconds); <code>iss</code>, <code>aud</code>, <code>azp</code>, <code>exp</code>, <code>nbf</code> and <code>iat</code> are checked with 60 seconds of clock skew, and tokens issued more than 10 minutes ago are refused.</li>
      <li>Discovery, JWKS and token requests only go to public addresses, are not redirected, and are limited to 8 seconds and 64 KiB. For a provider on your own network, or plain http while testing, set <code>SSO_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IDP=true</code> (separate from <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code>). Even then link-local and cloud metadata addresses (169.254.0.0/16, fe80::/10, fd00:ec2::254, 100.100.100.200), multicast and 0.0.0.0/8 are refused, connections stay pinned to the checked addresses, and the time, size and no-redirect limits still apply.</li>
      <li>A connection only signs people into its own workspace. Removing someone from the workspace is final: SSO does not add them back (remove them at the provider too).</li>
      <li>Signing out ends the Montral session; it does not sign you out of the identity provider.</li>
      <li>Owners see every configuration change, SSO sign-in and refused sign-in in the <a href="/docs/api#audit">audit log</a>.</li>
      <li>SAML is not supported; the reasons are in <code>docs/evidence/2026-11-10-oidc-sso.md</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="apns">iOS push notifications (APNs)</h2>
    <p>The Montral iOS app can receive alerts as push notifications. The server sends them through Apple's APNs, so it needs an APNs credential. Push is off until all four variables below are set; <code>GET /api/config</code> then reports <code>push.apns: true</code> and the <em>Mobile app (push)</em> channel type appears under Alerting.</p>
    <h3>What you need</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>An Apple Developer account and an App ID for the app, with the Push Notifications capability.</li>
      <li>An APNs Auth Key (a <code>.p8</code> file) from <strong>Certificates, Identifiers &amp; Profiles → Keys</strong>, with its <strong>Key ID</strong>.</li>
      <li>Your <strong>Team ID</strong> and the app's <strong>bundle id</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>APNS_KEY</code></td><td>The contents of the <code>.p8</code> file. A literal <code>\n</code> in place of line breaks is accepted, which is handy in <code>.env</code> files.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>APNS_KEY_ID</code></td><td>The key's 10-character id.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>APNS_TEAM_ID</code></td><td>Your Apple Developer team id.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>APNS_BUNDLE_ID</code></td><td>The app's bundle id, used as the APNs topic.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Docker</strong>: add the four variables to <code>.env</code> and run <code>docker compose up -d</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: in <code>apps/api</code> run <code>pnpm exec wrangler secret put APNS_KEY</code> (paste the whole file), then the same for <code>APNS_KEY_ID</code>, <code>APNS_TEAM_ID</code> and <code>APNS_BUNDLE_ID</code>, and redeploy the API Worker.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>How it works</h3>
    <p>People register their phone from the app; a <code>push</code> channel then alerts every member of the workspace who has a registered device, each in their own language. Registering a phone as an owner or admin creates a <em>Mobile app</em> channel for you if the workspace has none. Phones that Apple reports as no longer valid are forgotten automatically.</p>
    <p><strong>Important:</strong> an APNs key is tied to your Apple team and the app's bundle id, and a phone's token only works with the app that produced it. The official Montral app can therefore receive push only from the hosted service. On a self-hosted server push works for an app you build and sign yourself with your own bundle id and key. A relay that would let the official app receive push from self-hosted servers is not implemented.</p>
    <h2 id="custom-domains">Custom domains for status pages</h2>
    <p>A status page can be served on its own hostname, such as <code>status.example.com</code>, by the Docker (Node) server. <strong>Cloudflare Workers deployments do not support custom domains</strong>: the API refuses to set one there (<code>400</code>, code <code>custom_domain_unsupported</code>).</p>
    <p>Montral does not issue certificates. Your reverse proxy terminates TLS for the domain and forwards requests to Montral with the original <code>Host</code> header.</p>
    <h3>1. Claim and verify the domain</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>In the status page editor, open <strong>Custom domain</strong>, enter the hostname and save. Only owners and admins can do this.</li>
      <li>Create the TXT record shown: name <code>_montral-challenge.status.example.com</code>, value <code>montral-verify=…</code>, exactly as given.</li>
      <li>Press <strong>Verify</strong>. Montral looks the record up from the server and needs an exact match. Saving the domain again, even the same name, issues a new value and needs a new verification.</li>
      <li>DNS decides who holds a domain. Any page may name it, but only a page whose TXT record is published holds it, and only one page holds a domain at a time. When a domain changes hands, its new owner publishes their record and verifies: the domain moves to their page and the former page loses it, without that page's cooperation.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>2. Point the domain at your proxy</h3>
    <p>Add an <code>A</code>/<code>AAAA</code> or <code>CNAME</code> record for the hostname that points at your proxy, then add a site for it. With Caddy, which obtains the certificate itself and keeps the <code>Host</code> header by default:</p>
    <pre><code is:raw># Caddyfile
app.example.com {
	reverse_proxy montral:8080
}
status.example.com {
	reverse_proxy montral:8080
}</code></pre>
    <p>With nginx, keep the host: <code>proxy_set_header Host $host;</code>. If the proxy rewrites <code>Host</code>, Montral reads <code>X-Forwarded-Host</code> instead, but only from a trusted proxy (<code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code> and the proxy's address in <code>TRUST_PROXY_PEER_IPS</code>). From any other peer that header is ignored.</p>
    <h3>What the domain serves</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><code>/</code> is the status page. <code>/rss.xml</code>, <code>/maintenance.ics</code>, <code>/badge.svg</code> and <code>/llms.txt</code> are its feeds, and <code>/api/public/status/&lt;slug&gt;/…</code> keeps working for the page's own requests.</li>
      <li>A hostname that reaches the server but is neither the app's own address nor a verified status domain gets <code>404</code> on every path, so a domain pointed at your server before verification, or after its page or domain was removed, never shows the app or its sign-in. IP addresses, <code>localhost</code> and single-label names (such as compose service names) still reach the app.</li>
      <li>On a verified domain, every other path is <code>404</code>: the app, sign-in and sign-up, the private API, webhook receivers, docs and other pages. The domain never serves the signed-in app, and sign-in cookies are never read there.</li>
      <li>Public pages work as usual. Password pages show the password form, and unlocking sets an access cookie for that domain only. Members-only pages answer <code>404</code> on the custom domain, because sign-in lives on the main address. Share links still point at the main address.</li>
      <li>Changes made through the API apply at once on the server that handled them. With several servers, others pick a change up within 60 seconds.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Keep the TXT record</h3>
    <p>A verified domain keeps proving control. The server looks the TXT record up again about every 6 hours, and about every 30 minutes once a lookup failed (failing domains are checked first). A short DNS problem never takes the page offline: while a failure streak is young, the domain keeps serving and the editor shows when the streak started and why.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>If the record has been <strong>missing or holds another value</strong> for 24 hours, over at least three checks, verification is withdrawn and the domain answers <code>404</code>.</li>
      <li>If the domain's <strong>DNS cannot be reached at all</strong> (timeouts, SERVFAIL, dead nameservers), the page stays served for 7 days before verification is withdrawn. A streak that switches between unreachable DNS and a missing record starts over.</li>
      <li>The editor shows the reason for a withdrawal. Restore the record and press <strong>Verify</strong> to serve the domain again.</li>
      <li>The workspace's owners and admins get an email (in their language) when a domain fails its second re-check in a row, once per failing streak, and when it is withdrawn, once per withdrawal. Members get none. The emails need SMTP and appear in the alert log; a mail server that refuses one is retried twice, and the withdrawal itself never waits for mail.</li>
      <li>Several servers share the re-checks: each domain is claimed in the database, so it is looked up once per round. A withdrawal applies at once on the server that made it, and within 60 seconds on the others.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="oncall">On-call schedules and escalation</h2>
    <p>The <strong>On-call</strong> page (workspace section of the sidebar) holds schedules, overrides and escalation policies. Nothing needs configuring on the server beyond what alerts already use: people are paged by email at their account address (set up email delivery) and by push on phones they registered (needs <a href="#apns">APNs</a>).</p>
    <h3>Schedules</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A schedule has an IANA time zone and one or more <strong>layers</strong>. Each layer rotates through its people daily, weekly (on a chosen weekday) or every N hours, handing off at a local time from a start date. A layer can be limited to time windows, such as weekdays 09:00-17:00.</li>
      <li>Rotations shorter than 24 hours are measured in elapsed time from the first handoff, so every slot keeps its full length across daylight saving changes (a 1-hour rotation never loses anyone's hour on the spring night). Daily, weekly and longer rotations keep the local wall clock.</li>
      <li>A later layer covers the ones above it wherever it has someone on call; outside its windows the earlier layers show through.</li>
      <li>Handoffs follow the local clock, also across daylight saving changes: a handoff at a time the spring change skips (02:30 in New York) happens when the clocks jump; a time the autumn change repeats is used once, at its first occurrence. 30-minute changes (Lord Howe Island) work the same way.</li>
      <li><strong>Overrides</strong> put someone on call for a while and beat every layer; where they overlap, the latest created wins.</li>
      <li>Someone who leaves the workspace is skipped: their turn goes to the next person in the layer, and their overrides stop counting. Edit the layer to remove them for good.</li>
      <li>Each person can subscribe to their own shifts with a private iCalendar link (past week and next 60 days), and replace or turn it off at any time.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Who may change what</h3>
    <p>Owners and admins create and change schedules, layers, policies and anyone's overrides. Members see everything, including who is on call, and can add an override for themselves (to take a shift or swap) and remove one they added for themselves. Every change is in the audit log. Two people saving the same schedule at once cannot overwrite each other: the second save is refused with a conflict and shows what changed.</p>
    <h3>Escalation</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>An <strong>escalation policy</strong> is a list of steps. A step notifies channels, named people and whoever is on call on its schedules, then waits its timeout for someone to acknowledge before the next step. After the last step it can start over a few times, then stops.</li>
      <li>Choose a policy for a monitor in its settings. Its first step is paged as soon as an incident opens (the scheduler runs every minute). Monitors without a policy keep the project's escalation levels under Alerting, which can now also notify on-call schedules.</li>
      <li>Acknowledging an incident stops escalation, also for a page that was about to go out, and makes the acknowledger its owner if nobody owns it yet (it used to always reassign the incident). Resolving stops everything.</li>
      <li>A policy's first step does not page a channel again that already got the incident's down alert. Deleting a policy stops the escalation of its open incidents; new incidents of its monitors use the project's levels.</li>
      <li>A schedule keeps at most 500 overrides that have not ended (50 per person), each at most 90 days long and starting at most a year ahead. The calendar link can only be created while signed in, and replacing it says that the old link stopped working.</li>
      <li>Each step is sent once, even with several servers, and is written to the incident's timeline (team only) and to the audit log. Failed emails and pushes are retried like any alert and appear in the alert log.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="after">After install</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Create your first monitor, then a <a href="/docs/embed">status page</a> and, optionally, embed its state on your site.</li>
      <li>Automate with the <a href="/docs/api">API</a> or connect an agent through <a href="/docs/mcp">MCP</a>. Use your own domain in the examples.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div lang="zh-CN">
    <h1>自托管 Montral</h1>
    <p class="lede">在 Cloudflare Workers 或 Docker 上运行你自己的实例。两种方式使用同一套代码和一个由你掌控的 Postgres 数据库。</p>
    <p>二选一：</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#docker-zh"><strong>Docker</strong></a>：一个容器加 Postgres，任意机器可跑，最适合快速试用。</li>
      <li><a href="#cloudflare-zh"><strong>Cloudflare Workers</strong></a>：两个 Worker，加 Queue 和连接 Postgres 的 Hyperdrive，从 Cloudflare 网络发起检测。</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="docker-zh">Docker</h2>
    <p>一个容器同时运行 API、网页应用和检测调度器，compose 文件会一并启动 Postgres。</p>
    <h3>环境要求</h3>
    <ul><li>Docker 和 Compose v2</li><li>能访问被监控服务的机器</li></ul>
    <h3>启动</h3>
    <p><strong>从私有源码构建。</strong>Montral 尚未发布可下载的容器镜像或正式版本，需要先拥有私有 GitHub 仓库的访问权限。</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>git clone https://github.com/TheHalfMoon/Montral.git
cd Montral
cp .env.docker.example .env
# 在 .env 中设置 POSTGRES_PASSWORD 和 BETTER_AUTH_SECRET
docker compose up -d --build</code></pre>
    <p>打开 <code>http://localhost:8080</code> 注册即可。数据库结构在每次启动时自动迁移，数据保存在 <code>pgdata</code> 卷中。</p>
    <h3>绑定域名</h3>
    <p>在能终止 HTTPS 的反向代理（Caddy、nginx、Traefik、负载均衡器）后面运行，并把 <code>.env</code> 里的 <code>PUBLIC_URL</code> 设为公网地址，例如 <code>https://status.example.com</code>。Cookie、OAuth 和邮件里的链接都使用该值，用与配置不一致的域名访问会无法登录。</p>
    <h3>配置项（<code>.env</code>）</h3>
    <table class="vars">
      <thead><tr><th>变量</th><th>说明</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>POSTGRES_PASSWORD</code></td><td>必填。内置 Postgres 的密码。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code></td><td>必填。用于签名会话。用 <code>openssl rand -hex 32</code> 生成，并保持不变。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>PUBLIC_URL</code></td><td>公网地址，默认 <code>http://localhost:8080</code>。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>PORT</code></td><td>宿主机端口，默认 <code>8080</code>。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>DISABLE_SIGNUP</code></td><td>设为 <code>true</code> 关闭注册（请先创建好自己的账号），受邀的人仍可加入。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>LEGAL_LINKS</code></td><td>设为 <code>true</code> 后，注册表单会显示“创建账户即表示同意服务条款与隐私政策”。自带的 <code>/terms</code> 和 <code>/privacy</code> 描述的是 montral.invalid 托管服务，请先换成你自己的文本。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY</code><br /><code>TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY</code></td><td>两者都设置后，邮箱注册表单会显示 <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/">Cloudflare Turnstile</a> 验证，API 也会校验令牌。GitHub 登录不受影响。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>INVITE_TTL_DAYS</code></td><td>邀请有效天数，默认 7。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS</code></td><td>工作区审计事件保留天数，30 到 3650，默认 365。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CRON_SECRET</code></td><td>可选。允许外部调度器调用 <code>POST /internal/run-checks</code>；不设置则 <code>/internal/*</code> 保持关闭。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code></td><td>设为 <code>true</code> 以监控内网服务。默认拒绝指向私有、回环、链路本地地址（以及 compose 服务名这类单段主机名）的监控项和告警 Webhook，避免已注册用户探测你的内网。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CHECK_USER_AGENT</code></td><td>可选。HTTP 检查使用的 User-Agent。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>SELFCHECK_URLS</code></td><td>可选。检查失败时用来区分“目标故障”与“服务器断网”的网址，逗号分隔。不设置则使用三个公共站点；留空则关闭。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>PROBE_REGIONS</code><br><code>PROBE_SECRET</code></td><td>可选。用于<a href="#regions-zh">多区域检测</a>的远程探针。不设置时，所有检测都从本部署发起。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>EMAIL_FROM</code><br>+ 一种发信方式</td><td>可选的发信配置。方式为 <code>RESEND_API_KEY</code>、<code>SMTP_URL</code>（<code>smtps://user:pass@host:465</code>）或 <code>SMTP_HOST</code> / <code>SMTP_PORT</code> / <code>SMTP_USER</code> / <code>SMTP_PASS</code>（465 端口加 <code>SMTP_SECURE=true</code>）。不配置时邮件只写入容器日志。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code><br><code>GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code></td><td>可选，启用 GitHub 登录。<a href="#github-zh">配置与排错</a>。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN</code><br><code>PLAUSIBLE_SRC</code></td><td>可选的 Plausible 统计。域名为空则关闭。</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>运维</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>升级</strong>：目前无公开镜像；从私有源码更新时拉取新代码后执行 <code>docker compose up -d --build</code>。迁移在启动时自动运行。请先备份，详见<a href="#upgrade-zh">升级与回滚</a>。</li>
      <li><strong>PostgreSQL 版本</strong>：<code>docker-compose.yml</code> 固定了 <code>postgres:18.6-alpine</code> 及其数据目录。切勿把标签改为其他大版本：PostgreSQL 无法读取其他大版本的数据；固定数据目录后，较旧或较新的镜像会拒绝启动，而不是新建一个空数据库。跨大版本请通过导出和恢复迁移（<a href="/docs/backup">备份与恢复</a>）。</li>
      <li><strong>备份</strong>：<code>docker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U montral -Fc montral &gt; montral.dump</code>。恢复步骤见<a href="/docs/backup">备份与恢复</a>。</li>
      <li><strong>多个容器</strong>：检测通过 <code>FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED</code> 加租约，多个容器共用一个数据库也不会重复检测。</li>
      <li><strong>日志</strong>：<code>docker compose logs -f montral</code>。健康检查接口为 <code>/health</code>。</li>
      <li><strong>审计日志保留</strong>：工作区审计事件（控制台“工作区”中的“审计日志”）保留 <code>AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS</code> 天（默认 365，最少 30），由调度器每小时清理一次，Docker 和 Workers 相同。<code>audit_event</code> 表只能追加：数据库触发器拒绝 UPDATE、DELETE 和 TRUNCATE，唯一例外是 <code>montral_prune_audit</code> 保留期函数执行的删除，以及删除工作区时的级联删除。它防范的是应用程序错误，而不是数据库所有者，后者仍可删除该触发器。备份会像其他表一样包含此表。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 id="upgrade-zh">升级与回滚</h3>
    <p>迁移只能向前执行。下面每一步都在 CI（<code>montral-upgrade.yml</code>）中验证过：先用上一个候选发布版本建立一套包含用户、项目、监控、告警渠道、事件、状态页、Webhook 收件箱、维护窗口和 API 密钥的安装，再对它执行升级、回滚和从备份恢复。</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>先备份</strong>（应用可以保持运行）：<code>docker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U montral -Fc montral &gt; montral-pre-upgrade.dump</code>，再用 <code>pg_restore --list montral-pre-upgrade.dump | head</code> 检查文件。在确定不会回滚之前请一直保留它。</li>
      <li><strong>升级</strong>：更新源码后执行 <code>docker compose up -d --build</code>。新容器启动时会在接受请求之前，在一个事务中执行迁移；同时启动的多个容器会互相等待。数据、登录会话、API 密钥、分享链接、密码保护的状态页、自定义域名和 Webhook 接收地址都继续有效（前提是 <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> 不变）。</li>
      <li><strong>检查</strong>：<code>/health</code> 正常响应，可以登录，监控在一分钟内出现新的检测记录。</li>
    </ol>
    <p><strong>旧版本无法在升级后的数据库上启动</strong>，也不会改动任何数据。从这个版本起，程序会立即退出并提示 <code>database schema is newer than this Montral build; restore the pre-upgrade backup or run the newer build</code>。更早的版本（直到 17f55c1 候选发布版本）会重试约一分钟，然后以通用信息 <code>Database connection/migration unavailable after bounded startup retries</code> 退出，容器会不断重启。无论哪个版本，<code>pnpm --filter @montral/db-pg exec node migrate-plain.mjs --check</code> 都会给出原因：<code>Database migration history is ahead of this build</code>。因此，回到旧版本就意味着回到升级前的备份：</p>
    <pre><code>docker compose stop montral
docker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U montral -Fc montral &gt; montral-upgraded.dump   # 保存新版本写入的数据
docker compose exec postgres dropdb -U montral montral
docker compose exec postgres createdb -U montral montral
docker compose exec -T postgres pg_restore -U montral -d montral --no-owner &lt; montral-pre-upgrade.dump
# 检出之前的源码，然后
docker compose up -d --build</code></pre>
    <ul>
      <li>请像上面那样恢复到<strong>空</strong>数据库。不要用 <code>--clean</code> 把升级前的备份恢复到升级后的数据库上：升级新增的表和列不在备份里，会被留下，之后再次升级时可能因此失败。</li>
      <li>升级之后写入的内容（检测记录、事件、设置）不在升级前的备份里；额外的那份导出会保留它们，以便之后再次升级。</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>灾难恢复</strong>使用相同的命令：把最近的备份恢复到一个新的空数据库（<a href="/docs/backup#restore-zh">备份与恢复</a>），保持 <code>.env</code> 不变，然后启动应用；比备份更新的迁移会在启动时执行。CI 中的合成安装从数据库被删除到应用恢复服务并通过验证（建库、恢复、启动、登录并读回全部数据）用时约 2 秒；实际耗时随数据库大小增长，主要花在 <code>pg_restore</code> 上。</p>
    <h3 id="replicas-zh">负载均衡后的多个副本</h3>
    <p>如需更多容量或不中断地重启，可在同一个 PostgreSQL 上运行多个应用副本，并在前面放一个负载均衡器：</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>REPLICAS=2 docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.replicas.yml up -d --build</code></pre>
    <p>副本之间无需额外协调：定时检测、升级、告警投递和维护任务都在 PostgreSQL 中认领，因此每项总共只执行一次，而不是每个副本各执行一次；会话保存在 PostgreSQL 中，在任一副本登录都对所有副本有效。该叠加文件在前面放置 nginx（<code>docker/lb-nginx.conf</code>），会重新读取 Docker 的 DNS 以发现重启后的副本，连接被拒绝时改用另一个副本重试，并设置 <code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code>（因为它是前面唯一的代理）。升级时逐个重启副本（对每个容器执行 <code>docker restart</code>，等待其恢复健康），即可不丢请求。对外提供服务时请在负载均衡器前加 TLS（或在其上终止 TLS），并让 <code>DB_POOL_MAX</code> × 副本数小于 PostgreSQL 的 <code>max_connections</code>。CI 在每次变更时验证两个副本：请求分布到两个副本且共用一个会话、60 个并发 webhook 各只存储一次、滚动重启期间没有失败请求、每个 60 秒的检测在 330 秒内运行 3–8 次且没有被重复认领、一个失败的监控只打开一个事件。未验证：分布在不同主机上的副本，以及高可用 PostgreSQL。</p>
    <h3 id="ping-zh">Ping（ICMP）监控</h3>
    <p>Ping 监控调用服务器上的系统 <code>ping</code> 程序，因此只能在自托管 Node 服务器（Docker 或 <code>node server.mjs</code>）上运行；部署在 Cloudflare Workers 上时会拒绝创建。镜像基于 <code>node:22-alpine</code>，以非特权用户 <code>node</code> 运行，使用 BusyBox <code>ping</code> 和非特权 ICMP 套接字。Linux 只允许 <code>net.ipv4.ping_group_range</code> 中列出的用户组使用这类套接字；Docker 20.10 及更高版本在每个容器中都将其设为 <code>0 2147483647</code>，因此无需额外配置。如果使用较旧的引擎、其他容器运行时，或主机默认值受限，请在 <code>docker-compose.yml</code> 的 <code>montral</code> 服务中加入：</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>    sysctls:
      net.ipv4.ping_group_range: "0 2147483647"</code></pre>
    <p>该设置作用于容器自己的网络命名空间，不影响主机；不能与 <code>network_mode: host</code> 同时使用，此时请在主机上设置。若 <code>ping</code> 不存在或不被允许发送 ICMP，检测结果为“不确定”（“Ping unavailable on this server”，属于服务器而非目标的问题）：不会发送告警，服务器日志只提示一次。每次检测只解析一次主机名，除非设置了 <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code>，否则拒绝私有和内网地址（与 TCP 监控相同），然后 ping 经过验证的 IP 地址，优先使用 IPv4。IPv6 目标需要容器具备 IPv6 连接（Docker 网络默认只有 IPv4，除非启用 IPv6）；否则检测结果记为无结论。在 Docker 之外，Linux 上 iputils 的 <code>ping</code> 通常具有 <code>cap_net_raw</code> 能力或依赖同一 sysctl；macOS 与 Windows 的 <code>ping</code> 无需额外设置。</p>

    <h3 id="browser-checks-zh">浏览器检测（多步骤流程）</h3>
    <p>浏览器监控在无头 Chromium 中运行由固定步骤组成的流程（打开页面、填写表单、点击、等待、检查文本、网址或状态码）。该功能默认关闭。在 Docker 中，它运行在独立的 <strong>browser-runner</strong> 服务里，绝不在应用容器中运行：</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>echo "BROWSER_RUNNER_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> .env
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.browser.yml up -d --build</code></pre>
    <p>应用仍使用默认镜像（不含浏览器）。覆盖文件新增 <code>browser-runner</code> 服务，由 Dockerfile 的 <code>browser-runner</code> 目标构建（基于 Debian slim，包含固定 Playwright 版本对应的 Chromium headless shell，约 1.2 GB；Playwright 不支持 Alpine），并通过 <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_URL</code> 在应用中启用浏览器检测。</p>
    <p><strong>为什么要单独的服务。</strong>被监控的页面是来自互联网、在 Chromium 中运行的代码。假如它在应用容器里突破了 Chromium 的沙箱，就能读取服务器的环境变量（数据库地址、认证密钥）。runner 的设计让这种突破得不到任何有价值的东西：</p>
    <ul>
      <li>它拿不到 <code>DATABASE_URL</code>、<code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> 或任何其他应用配置，只有 <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_TOKEN</code> 和它自己的限制参数。</li>
      <li>它只接入一个仅与应用共享的内部网络（没有出口），以及一个通往互联网的独立出口网络；不接入数据库所在的网络，因此从它那里既无法解析也无法路由到 PostgreSQL。</li>
      <li>它只接受用 <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_TOKEN</code> 签名的任务：对方法、路径、时间戳、随机 nonce 和请求体做 HMAC-SHA256。超过 60 秒或重放的请求会被拒绝，且无论原因如何响应都相同；请求体最大 512 KB，每个响应也带签名。一个任务只包含一次运行的流程以及该次运行所需的密钥；这些密钥用从令牌派生的密钥加密，任务的其余部分只签名不加密，因此任务网络必须保持内部。应用会按严格的结构校验每个响应，只保存固定的信息。</li>
      <li>它以 Docker 的 init 作为 PID 1（<code>init: true</code>，回收孤儿进程），以非特权用户运行，配置 <code>cap_drop: [ALL]</code>、<code>no-new-privileges</code>、只读根文件系统、限制大小的 <code>/tmp</code> 和 <code>/dev/shm</code>，并限制进程数（1024）、内存（2 GB）和 CPU（2）。</li>
      <li>它的 seccomp 配置是 Docker 默认配置，只额外允许 <code>clone</code>、<code>unshare</code>、<code>setns</code> 和 <code>chroot</code>（<code>docker/browser-runner-seccomp.json</code>）。这正是 Chromium 自身沙箱建立用户、PID 和网络命名空间所需的调用；Docker 拒绝的其他一切仍被拒绝。</li>
      <li>如需更强的隔离，可在安装了 gVisor 的主机上给该服务加上 <code>runtime: runsc</code>。</li>
    </ul>
    <p>在 runner 内部，每次检测仍使用独立的短生命周期 worker 进程，拥有专属临时目录（结束后删除），以及配置为空的全新 Chromium，因此 Cookie、存储和缓存不会在检测或工作区之间传递。Chromium 唯一的出口是该 worker 内的代理：每个主机名只解析一次，并且只连接经过验证的地址，从而杜绝 DNS 重绑定。除非设置 <code>BROWSER_CHECK_ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS=true</code>，否则拒绝私有和内网地址；<code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code> 不会对浏览器开放这些地址。回环地址、链路本地地址、云元数据地址、<code>localhost</code>、runner 自己的地址和应用的地址始终被拒绝。不经代理的 WebRTC 流量和 QUIC 均已关闭。流程不能运行你自己的 JavaScript。</p>
    <p><strong>不使用 Docker</strong>（<code>node server.mjs</code>）时，浏览器检测也可以在应用的进程树内运行：安装固定版本的 Chromium（<code>pnpm --filter @montral/e2e exec playwright install --with-deps chromium</code>，或设置 <code>BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH</code>），用 <code>pnpm --filter @montral/api build:browser-worker</code> 在服务端旁构建 worker，并设置 <code>BROWSER_CHECKS=enabled</code>。这样 Chromium 与服务器以同一用户运行，一旦突破沙箱就可能读取服务器的密钥。建议改用 runner：以另一个用户、在没有应用环境变量的情况下运行 <code>node browser-runner.mjs</code>（用 <code>pnpm --filter @montral/api build:browser-runner</code> 构建），并在应用中设置 <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_URL</code> 和 <code>BROWSER_RUNNER_TOKEN</code>。生产环境中不能关闭 Chromium 沙箱：只有当 <code>NODE_ENV</code> 为 <code>development</code> 时才接受 <code>BROWSER_CHECK_SANDBOX=off</code>，否则浏览器检测将不可用。在 runner（或本服务器）成功启动过一次 Chromium 之前，创建浏览器监控会被拒绝；该结果缓存十分钟。</p>
    <p><strong>公平性、限制与资源规划。</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>浏览器监控最快每 5 分钟检测一次；更短的间隔会被调高。</li>
      <li>同时运行 <code>MAX_BROWSER_CHECKS</code> 个浏览器检测（默认 2，最多 16），且每个工作区同时最多一个，避免单个租户占满所有名额。另有少量检测最多等待 15 秒；再多的检测会被推迟。同一工作区中同时到期的浏览器监控在一个队列任务中依次运行，该任务最多花 2 分钟（只有最坏情况仍能放进预算时才开始一个检测，其余推迟），且一个工作区的浏览器检测最多占用一个队列名额。浏览器检测的额度在旅程开始前扣除；没有额度的工作区不会启动任何旅程（不记录任何内容，与其他监控相同）。被推迟的检测会在约一分钟内重试，并退还额度；它在监控上每个间隔最多显示一条推迟记录，因此重试不会把真实运行挤出历史。运行环境无法执行的检测（runner 无法连接或拒绝、Chromium 无法启动）记录为错误运行，同样退还额度。连续 3 次运行环境错误，或推迟已持续该监控的 3 个间隔（从推迟开始时计算，与间隔长短无关）时，监控显示为“未检测”；工作区的所有者和管理员随后会收到一封列出所有未检测浏览器监控的汇总邮件，每个工作区每小时最多一封（告警日志中按项目各记一条，只列出该项目的监控）。下一次真实运行会清除该状态；暂停、恢复或修改监控检测的内容（间隔、旅程、目标）也会清除。监控页面会显示浏览器运行环境的状态及最近一次问题。</li>
      <li>每个并发检测约需 600 MB 内存（实测：简单流程整个进程树的峰值为 609 MiB）和最多一个 CPU 核心：默认 2 个并发时为 2 GB 和 2 个核心，即 runner 上配置的限制。</li>
      <li><code>BROWSER_CHECK_MAX_RSS_MB</code>（默认 1024）限制单次检测整个进程树（worker、Chromium 及其子进程）的内存，在 Linux 上每 250 毫秒采样一次；超过后整个进程树被终止，检测以“Browser check exceeded its memory limit”失败。每次检测另有 30 秒 CPU 时间上限，以及流程超时（最多 60 秒）加上启动与关闭的余量；页面 JavaScript 的堆上限为 256 MB。worker 崩溃时也不会遗留 Chromium：命令行中带有该检测配置目录的所有进程都会被一并终止。</li>
      <li>每个页面每个连接最多传输 10 MB，每次检测最多 25 MB，最多 256 个连接。</li>
      <li>运行记录按监控项保留：最近 50 次；截图（仅在监控要求时于失败时保存，最大 200 KB，已遮盖密钥和密码字段）只保留其中最近 5 次；超过 14 天的记录一律删除。使用了密钥的运行，其截图只向所有者和管理员显示（按每次运行判断）；修改监控的密钥会删除这些截图。</li>
    </ul>
    <p>浏览器监控的密钥使用由 <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> 派生的密钥加密，并与所属工作区、监控项和名称绑定。更换 <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> 后这些密钥将无法读取：相关步骤以“secret is not set”失败，直到重新填写。浏览器检测不能在 Cloudflare Workers 上运行；在 Windows 和 macOS 上不测量内存和 CPU 限制（时间限制仍然有效），生产环境请在 Linux 上运行。</p>

    <h2 id="cloudflare-zh">Cloudflare Workers</h2>
    <p>两个 Worker：<code>montral-api</code>（<code>/api/*</code> 下的 API、每分钟的 cron 和队列消费者）和 <code>montral-web</code>（站点本身，通过 service binding 访问 API）。</p>
    <h3>环境要求</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>一个 Cloudflare 账号，以及托管在 Cloudflare 的域名。只有下文的 Queue 模式需要 <strong>Workers 付费版</strong>；免费版可用内联模式，适合小规模</li>
      <li>一个 Cloudflare 能访问的 Postgres 数据库。通过 Hyperdrive 连接，所以 Neon、Supabase、RDS 或自建均可</li>
      <li>Node.js 22+ 和 pnpm（<code>corepack enable</code> 会装好指定版本）。Wrangler 随项目安装，在 <code>apps/api</code> 中执行 <code>pnpm exec wrangler login</code> 登录</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>1. 获取代码</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>git clone https://github.com/TheHalfMoon/Montral.git
cd montral
pnpm install</code></pre>
    <h3>2. 选择检测运行方式，并创建 Hyperdrive</h3>
    <p>检测有两种运行模式，是否保留 <code>apps/api/wrangler.jsonc</code> 里的 <code>queues</code> 配置块决定使用哪一种，只是配置切换，不需要改代码。</p>
    <table class="vars">
      <thead><tr><th>模式</th><th>套餐</th><th>说明</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Queue</strong>（默认）</td><td>Workers <strong>付费版</strong></td><td>cron 把到期的监控项按每 25 个一条消息放入 Queue，由消费者并行执行，可扩展到数千个监控项。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>内联</strong></td><td>免费版或付费版</td><td>不用 Queue。每分钟的 cron 自己执行检测，每次最多 <strong>40 个监控项</strong>，受免费版 50 个子请求和 10 ms CPU 限制，仅适合小规模。</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><strong>Queue 模式</strong>（配置文件默认如此）：创建一次队列。</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>pnpm exec wrangler queues create montral-checks</code></pre>
    <p><strong>内联模式</strong>：从 <code>apps/api/wrangler.jsonc</code> 中删除整个 <code>"queues"</code> 配置块，并跳过上面的命令。没有绑定队列时 Worker 会自动改为内联执行。</p>
    <p>然后创建 Hyperdrive，把得到的 id 填进 <code>apps/api/wrangler.jsonc</code> 的 <code>hyperdrive</code> 配置块：</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>pnpm exec wrangler hyperdrive create montral-prod --connection-string="postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db"</code></pre>
    <h3>3. 创建数据库结构</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db" pnpm db:migrate</code></pre>
    <p>它不会执行 <code>CREATE SCHEMA</code>，所以没有数据库级 <code>CREATE</code> 权限的角色也能运行。每次升级后重新执行即可。</p>
    <p>升级前可以只读检查数据库：<code>DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db" pnpm --filter @montral/db-pg exec node migrate-plain.mjs --check</code> 会验证已执行的迁移历史与当前版本一致，并列出将要执行的迁移，不会修改数据库。迁移在同一个事务中执行，因此不支持 <code>CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY</code>，同一次运行中也不能使用前一个迁移刚新增的枚举值。</p>
    <h3>4. 把配置指向你的域名</h3>
    <p>在 <code>apps/api/wrangler.jsonc</code> 中设置 <code>routes</code>（<code>你的域名/api/*</code>）、<code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code> 和 <code>WEB_ORIGIN</code>（都填 <code>https://你的域名</code>）以及 <code>EMAIL_FROM</code>。删除 <code>placement</code> 块，或改成你自己的数据库主机。</p>
    <p>在 <code>apps/web/wrangler.jsonc</code> 中设置自定义域名的 <code>routes</code>，以及 <code>PRODUCT_URL</code>（"Powered by" 链接的目标，填你自己的地址）。</p>
    <h3>5. 密钥</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>cd apps/api
pnpm exec wrangler secret put BETTER_AUTH_SECRET     # openssl rand -hex 32
pnpm exec wrangler secret put CRON_SECRET            # 任意足够长的随机字符串，保护 /internal/*
# 可选：GITHUB_CLIENT_ID 和 GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET，用于 GitHub 登录</code></pre>
    <h3>6. 部署</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>cd apps/api &amp;&amp; pnpm exec wrangler deploy
cd ../web &amp;&amp; pnpm build &amp;&amp; pnpm exec wrangler deploy</code></pre>
    <p>务必先部署 API：web Worker 依赖它。然后打开你的域名注册即可。</p>
    <h3>配置项</h3>
    <table class="vars vars-3">
      <thead><tr><th>位置</th><th>变量</th><th>说明</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code><br><code>WEB_ORIGIN</code></td><td>站点公网地址，用于 Cookie、OAuth 和邮件链接。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>EMAIL_FROM</code></td><td>发件地址。需在 Cloudflare Email Sending 中接入该域名；不配置则邮件只写日志。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>INVITE_TTL_DAYS</code></td><td>邀请有效天数，默认 7。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS</code></td><td>工作区审计事件保留天数，30 到 3650，默认 365。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code></td><td>设为 <code>true</code> 允许监控项和告警 Webhook 指向私有地址，默认拒绝。Cloudflare Workers 本身无法访问私有网段，此项主要影响 Docker 部署。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars + secret</td><td><code>PROBE_REGIONS</code>, <code>PROBE_SECRET</code></td><td>可选。用于<a href="#regions-zh">多区域检测</a>的远程探针。区域列表放在 <code>vars</code>，共享密钥用 <code>wrangler secret put PROBE_SECRET</code> 设置。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>DISABLE_SIGNUP</code></td><td>设为 <code>true</code> 关闭注册（邮箱与 GitHub 均适用）。请先创建好自己的账号；之后只有持有待处理邀请的人还能注册。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars</td><td><code>LEGAL_LINKS</code></td><td>设为 <code>true</code> 后，注册表单会显示“创建账户即表示同意服务条款与隐私政策”。自带的 <code>/terms</code> 和 <code>/privacy</code> 描述的是 montral.invalid 托管服务，请先换成你自己的文本。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api vars + secret</td><td><code>TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY</code>、<code>TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY</code></td><td>可选。站点密钥放进 API 的 <code>vars</code>，私钥用 <code>wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY</code> 设置；之后邮箱注册需要通过 Turnstile 验证。两者必须同时设置。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>api secrets</td><td><code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code><br><code>CRON_SECRET</code></td><td>见第 5 步。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>web vars</td><td><code>PRODUCT_URL</code></td><td>状态页 "Powered by" 链接的目标。</td></tr>
        <tr><td>web vars</td><td><code>PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN</code><br><code>PLAUSIBLE_SRC</code></td><td>可选统计。未设置域名则关闭。</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>检测如何运行</h3>
    <p>cron 每分钟触发一次并租约到期的监控项。Queue 模式下每 25 个打包成一条消息放入 <code>montral-checks</code> 队列，由消费者执行每个分组，记录结果、开启和解决事件并发送告警。内联模式下这些都由 cron 自己完成，每次最多 40 个监控项。</p>
    <h3>升级</h3>
    <p>拉取新代码，重新执行迁移（只会应用新增的部分），然后先部署 API、再部署 web Worker。</p>
    <h3>之后切换模式</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>免费版升级到付费版</strong>：升级套餐，恢复 <code>queues</code> 配置块，执行 <code>pnpm exec wrangler queues create montral-checks</code>，再 <code>pnpm exec wrangler deploy</code> API。</li>
      <li><strong>付费版降到免费版</strong>：删除 <code>queues</code> 配置块并重新部署 API，之后可以删除队列。</li>
    </ul>
    <p>不涉及数据迁移，监控项、历史记录和事件都不受影响。</p>

    <h2 id="regions-zh">多区域检测</h2>
    <p>默认情况下，监控项从 Montral 自身所在位置发起检测。想从多个地点检测，可把 <code>apps/probe</code> 中的小型探针部署到几个区域，再把它们的地址告诉 API。只有你为某个监控项指定了区域，才会使用探针；其他监控项仍从本部署发起，因此不主动开启就不会有任何变化。结论如何得出、应用里能看到什么，见<a href="/docs/regions">多区域检测</a>。</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>部署探针</strong>到你想让检测发起的每个地点。探针是个小服务，按请求执行一次检测，有两种运行方式，可任选或混用：对 API 来说每个探针只是一个 URL。</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>方式 A：Docker 或任意 Node 主机</h3>
    <p>探针就是一个普通的 Node 服务，可以跑在任何国家的任意 VPS 或机器上。镜像在仓库根目录构建：</p>
    <pre><code is:raw>docker build -f apps/probe/Dockerfile -t montral-probe .
docker run -d --restart unless-stopped -p 8787:8787 \
  -e PROBE_SECRET=&lt;一段足够长的随机字符串&gt; -e PROBE_REGION=sao-paulo \
  montral-probe</code></pre>
    <p><code>apps/probe/docker-compose.yml</code> 对它做了封装（当前仅从私有仓库构建镜像，未发布公共镜像），并可用 Caddy 自动加上 HTTPS：<code is:raw>PROBE_DOMAIN=probe-sao.example.com docker compose --profile tls up -d</code>。不用 Docker 时，运行 <code>pnpm --filter @montral/probe build:node</code>，再 <code>PROBE_SECRET=… node apps/probe/dist/server.mjs</code>（Node 22）。API 需要 <code>https</code> 地址，所以请把探针放在反向代理或自带的 Caddy 后面。Docker 和 Node 探针对 <code>GET /</code> 返回 <code is:raw>{"ok":true,"region":"…"}</code>，可用于健康检查；Vercel 上同样的响应在 <code>/api/probe/&lt;id&gt;</code>，根路径是 404。</p>
    <p>配置项：<code>PROBE_SECRET</code>（必填）、<code>PROBE_REGION</code>（标签）、<code>PORT</code>（默认 8787）、<code>HOST</code>（默认 0.0.0.0）、<code>CHECK_USER_AGENT</code>（与 API 上的含义相同）。默认拒绝私有和内部地址；只有在该探针上设置 <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS=true</code> 才允许，这样就可以把探针放在办公室或家里的内网中，检测内部服务。请只对确实位于被监控网络内的探针这样做。</p>
    <h3>方式 B：Vercel，一次部署多个区域</h3>
    <p>自带的构建会为每个区域生成一个函数（<code>apps/probe/regions.json</code>，默认：弗吉尼亚、旧金山、法兰克福、新加坡、东京）。在 Vercel 项目上设置 <code>PROBE_SECRET</code>，在 <code>apps/probe</code> 中运行 <code>pnpm build:vercel</code>，再 <code>vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod</code>。让函数在多个区域运行，需要允许这一点的 Vercel 套餐。</p>
    <ol start="2">
      <li><strong>告诉 API。</strong>把同一个密钥设为 <code>PROBE_SECRET</code>，并用 JSON 在 <code>PROBE_REGIONS</code> 中列出区域：</li>
    </ol>
    <pre><code is:raw>PROBE_SECRET=&lt;与探针相同的密钥&gt;
PROBE_REGIONS={"us-east":"https://probe.example.app/api/probe/us-east","eu-central":"https://probe.example.app/api/probe/eu-central","ap-southeast":{"url":"https://probe.example.app/api/probe/ap-southeast","name":"Singapore"}}</code></pre>
    <p>键是你自己定的区域 id（小写字母、数字和连字符）。值可以是 URL，或 <code is:raw>{ "url", "name" }</code> 以设置在应用中显示的名称。URL 必须是 <code>https</code>。区域列表会出现在应用和 <code>GET /api/regions</code> 中，监控项可在套餐上限内选择多个区域。</p>
    <h3>行为说明</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>只有 <strong>HTTP、TCP 和 WebSocket</strong> 监控项可以使用区域。其他类型和心跳始终从本部署发起。</li>
      <li>选择多个区域时，只有<strong>多数应答的区域</strong>都失败才判定为失败，单个区域的线路问题不会产生事件。各区域的结果都会保留，监控详情页按区域显示可用率和延迟。</li>
      <li>探针无法连通不算检测失败：它不参与表决；所有探针都没有应答时，改为从本部署发起检测，因此探针故障不会让监控失明。</li>
      <li>每个区域各计一次检查额度。也可以在监控详情页（或 <code>POST /api/monitors/:id/check</code> 并传 <code>region</code>）从某一个区域单次发起请求；该请求不会被记录，也不会改变监控状态。</li>
      <li>探针只接受签名请求（对时间戳与请求体做 HMAC-SHA256，允许 60 秒偏差），并且无论签名是否有效，都会拒绝私有、回环和链路本地地址（除非该探针的运维者自己打开 <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code>），因此不会变成开放代理。</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="github-zh">GitHub 登录</h2>
    <p>“使用 GitHub 继续”是可选功能，配置 GitHub OAuth App 后才会启用。未配置时，网页和移动应用都不会显示 GitHub 按钮，邮箱登录照常使用。</p>
    <h3>1. 创建 OAuth App</h3>
    <p>在 GitHub 打开 <strong>Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps → New OAuth App</strong>（组织账号在其对应页面）。填写：</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Homepage URL</strong>：你的公网地址，例如 <code>https://status.example.com</code>。</li>
      <li><strong>Authorization callback URL</strong>：必须精确为 <code>&lt;BETTER_AUTH_URL&gt;/api/auth/callback/github</code>。Docker 中 <code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code> 即 <code>PUBLIC_URL</code>；Cloudflare 上是 API Worker 的 <code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code> 变量，即站点公网地址（API 在同一域名的 <code>/api</code> 下）。例如 <code>https://status.example.com/api/auth/callback/github</code>。</li>
    </ul>
    <p>创建 Client secret，并保存这两个值。</p>
    <h3>2. 设置两个变量</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Docker</strong>：把 <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code> 和 <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code> 写入 <code>.env</code>，然后执行 <code>docker compose up -d</code>。</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>：在 <code>apps/api</code> 中执行 <code>pnpm exec wrangler secret put GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code> 和 <code>pnpm exec wrangler secret put GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code>，然后重新部署 API Worker。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>3. 验证</h3>
    <pre><code is:raw>curl https://status.example.com/api/config
# "auth": { ..., "github": true, ... }</code></pre>
    <p>两个变量必须同时设置，只设一个时 <code>github</code> 仍为 <code>false</code>。之后已登录的用户可以在 <strong>账号 → 已关联的账号</strong> 中关联或取消关联 GitHub，GitHub 邮箱可以与账号邮箱不同。只有 GitHub 报告该邮箱已验证时，GitHub 登录才会按邮箱匹配已有账号；账号始终至少保留一种登录方式。<code>DISABLE_SIGNUP</code> 同样适用于首次 GitHub 登录。</p>
    <p>首次 GitHub 登录会创建账号和个人工作区，此时没有密码。需要密码时，用 GitHub 邮箱走“忘记密码”即可设置（需要已配置发信）。这类账号删除时不需要密码，只要求最近登录过。</p>
    <p>移动应用使用同一个提供方：它从 <code>/api/config</code> 读取 <code>auth.github</code>，并通过 <code>/api/auth/native/github</code> 走同一个 OAuth App，无需额外注册（见<a href="/docs/api#native-signin-zh">原生登录</a>）。</p>
    <h3>排错</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>“redirect_uri is not associated with this application”</strong>：OAuth App 中的回调地址与 <code>&lt;BETTER_AUTH_URL&gt;/api/auth/callback/github</code> 不一致（协议、主机、端口或路径）。请在 GitHub 中修改。</li>
      <li><strong>回调跳到了错误的主机</strong>：<code>BETTER_AUTH_URL</code>（Docker 中为 <code>PUBLIC_URL</code>）设置有误，常见是仍为 <code>localhost</code>。改成公网地址并重启。</li>
      <li><strong>位于反向代理之后</strong>：在代理处终止 HTTPS，并传递原始的 <code>Host</code> 与 <code>X-Forwarded-Proto</code> 请求头。给 GitHub 填写的应是上面配置的公网地址。</li>
      <li><strong>看不到按钮</strong>：<code>/api/config</code> 显示 <code>github: false</code>，说明变量为空或服务未重启。</li>
      <li><strong>“Sign-ups are closed”</strong>：已设置 <code>DISABLE_SIGNUP=true</code>；请先邀请对方，或在已有账号中关联 GitHub。</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="sso-zh">单点登录（OpenID Connect）</h2>
    <p>Montral 可以通过任意 OpenID Connect 身份提供商登录。有两种设置方式，可以同时使用：</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>按工作区</strong>（无需服务器配置）：工作区所有者在<strong>设置 → 单点登录</strong>中添加连接。邮箱属于该工作区<em>已验证</em>域名的用户，首次登录时会自动获得该工作区的账号。</li>
      <li><strong>全实例</strong>：运维者设置 <code>OIDC_ISSUER</code>、<code>OIDC_CLIENT_ID</code> 和 <code>OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET</code>（可选 <code>OIDC_ALLOWED_DOMAINS</code>）。首次登录会像注册一样创建普通账号及其个人工作区，并遵循 <code>DISABLE_SIGNUP</code>。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>1. 在身份提供商处注册 Montral</h3>
    <p>创建一个 OpenID Connect（OAuth 2.0）<em>Web 应用</em> / 机密客户端：</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>重定向 URI</strong>：<code>&lt;BETTER_AUTH_URL&gt;/api/auth/sso/callback</code>，必须完全一致（Docker 中为 <code>&lt;PUBLIC_URL&gt;/api/auth/sso/callback</code>）。设置页面会显示该地址。Montral 不接受其他重定向目标。</li>
      <li><strong>授权方式</strong>：授权码，带 PKCE（S256）。<strong>Scope</strong>：<code>openid email profile</code>。</li>
      <li><strong>客户端认证</strong>：客户端密钥（HTTP Basic 或 POST 正文）。</li>
      <li><strong>id_token 签名</strong>：非对称算法（RS256、PS256、ES256、EdDSA 等）。HMAC（HS256）和 <code>none</code> 会被拒绝。</li>
      <li>id_token 必须包含 <code>email</code> 和 <code>email_verified: true</code>（布尔值）。缺少它的登录一律拒绝，且有意不提供“无此声明也信任邮箱”的设置：未验证的地址会让身份提供商冒认任何账号。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>2. 配置连接</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>颁发者（Issuer）URL</strong>：提供商的颁发者，必须与其 <code>/.well-known/openid-configuration</code> 中的名称逐字符一致。可以用<strong>测试连接</strong>检查。</li>
      <li><strong>客户端 ID</strong> 和<strong>客户端密钥</strong>。密钥以加密形式保存（AES-256-GCM，密钥由 <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> 派生），之后不会再显示，API 不会返回，也不会写入审计日志。更换 <code>BETTER_AUTH_SECRET</code> 后已保存的密钥将无法解密，需要重新填写。更换颁发者或客户端 ID 时必须重新填写密钥；密钥只会发送到填写时提供商指明的令牌端点：如果之后发现文档指向另一个端点，登录会停止（<code>connection_misconfigured</code>），直到所有者重新保存密钥。</li>
      <li><strong>邮箱域名</strong>：为每个域名发布页面上显示的 TXT 记录（<code>_montral-challenge.&lt;域名&gt;</code>），然后点击<strong>验证</strong>。只有已验证的域名可以登录，且同一实例中一个域名只能被一个工作区验证。请保留该记录：系统大约每 6 小时重新查询一次（失败时每 30 分钟一次），记录缺失或内容不符持续 24 小时（或 DNS 无法访问持续 7 天）后撤销验证。被撤销的域名不能再用于登录，其他工作区发布自己的记录后即可验证它。</li>
      <li><strong>新成员的角色</strong>：成员（默认）或管理员，绝不会是所有者。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>示例设置</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Keycloak</strong>：颁发者 <code>https://keycloak.example.com/realms/&lt;realm&gt;</code>。创建客户端，开启 <em>Client authentication</em> 和 <em>Standard flow</em>，将 <em>Valid redirect URIs</em> 设为上述重定向 URI，并确保用户的 <em>Email verified</em> 为开启。</li>
      <li><strong>Authentik</strong>：颁发者 <code>https://authentik.example.com/application/o/&lt;应用 slug&gt;/</code>（带末尾斜杠）。创建 OAuth2/OpenID 提供程序（机密客户端，设置签名密钥以使用 RS256）和应用。Authentik 默认的邮箱映射可能返回 <code>email_verified: false</code>；只有在 Authentik 确实验证过邮箱时才映射为 true。</li>
      <li><strong>Microsoft Entra ID</strong>：颁发者 <code>https://login.microsoftonline.com/&lt;租户 ID&gt;/v2.0</code>（单租户；多租户的 <code>common</code> 端点没有固定的颁发者，不受支持）。注册类型为 <em>Web</em> 的应用，填写重定向 URI 并创建客户端密钥，添加可选声明 <code>email</code>。Entra ID 默认不发送 <code>email_verified</code>，因此在发送之前登录都会被拒绝：可通过声明映射策略添加它，并且只对租户中已验证域名的地址输出 <code>true</code>；或在 Entra ID 前面用 Keycloak 或 Authentik 作为中转来声明它。</li>
      <li><strong>Google Workspace</strong>：颁发者 <code>https://accounts.google.com</code>。在 Google Cloud 中创建类型为 <em>Web 应用</em> 的 OAuth 客户端 ID 并填写重定向 URI，然后在 Montral 中验证你的 Workspace 域名。任何 Google 账号都能到达授权页面，因此由已验证的域名决定谁可以登录。</li>
      <li><strong>Okta</strong>：颁发者 <code>https://&lt;你的组织&gt;.okta.com</code>（或自定义授权服务器，例如 <code>https://&lt;你的组织&gt;.okta.com/oauth2/default</code>）。创建使用授权码方式的 OIDC <em>Web Application</em>，并填写重定向 URI。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>已有账号</h3>
    <p>已经用相同邮箱注册过 Montral 的用户<strong>不会</strong>被自动登录或关联，即使域名已验证：否则身份提供商（或控制它的工作区所有者）就能接管任何邮箱相同的账号。他们会看到“使用此邮箱的账号已存在”，只需关联一次：先照常登录（密码、两步验证或 GitHub），打开<strong>账户 → 单点登录</strong>，选择<strong>关联单点登录</strong>。身份提供商必须确认该账号本身的邮箱地址。之后即可通过 SSO 登录。关联只是一种登录方式，不代表成员身份：尚未加入工作区的人仍需要邀请。没有 Montral 账号的用户会在首次登录时自动创建（即时开通），邮箱为已验证状态，没有密码，并成为该连接所属工作区的成员。将某人移出工作区时，会退出其登录、删除其与该工作区连接的 SSO 关联，并记录这次移出（其邮箱地址和 SSO 身份），因此 SSO 不会再让他登录或重新加入，即使他删除账号后也不会再次自动开通；要回来需要接受发往其邮箱的新邀请（待处理或已取消的邀请不会解除限制）。</p>
    <p>同理，对于拥有 SSO 身份或属于要求 SSO 的工作区的账号，社交登录（GitHub）不会因为邮箱相同就自动关联：请在登录状态下从<strong>账户 → 已连接账号</strong>中连接。</p>
    <h3>要求使用单点登录</h3>
    <p>开启<strong>要求此工作区使用单点登录</strong>后，除所有者外的所有成员只能通过此连接使用该工作区：他们的密码、GitHub 等登录方式（包括运维者配置的全实例提供商）都会被拒绝；开启时会退出他们的其他会话，任何不是由此连接创建的会话访问该工作区时都返回 <code>403</code>，Better Auth 自身处理的操作（邀请、角色、当前工作区、智能体授权、API 密钥）也同样如此。<strong>所有者是应急账号</strong>：保留密码登录，确保身份提供商故障或配置错误时工作区不会被锁死。请为该账号设置强密码并开启两步验证。要求使用 SSO 需要至少一个已验证域名；关闭连接会同时解除该要求。他们的 API 密钥只有在通过此连接登录的会话中创建时才能用于该工作区；智能体（OAuth）令牌只在授权它的 SSO 会话仍处于登录状态时有效；其他的会被拒绝（<code>403</code>，解除要求后密钥恢复）。授权智能体或导出账户需要满足此人所属的每一个要求 SSO 的工作区（因此同时属于两个使用不同提供商且都要求 SSO 的工作区的人无法进行这两项操作）。以其他方式登录时接受邀请的人会成为成员，但在通过 SSO 登录之前无法在该工作区进行任何操作（该工作区也不会出现在其工作区列表中，仅限成员的状态页对其保持隐藏）。更换连接的颁发者或客户端会退出该连接创建的会话。所有者本人的会话、密钥和智能体不与 SSO 绑定。</p>
    <p><strong>人员离职：</strong>不支持 SCIM，因此在身份提供商处移除某人只会阻止新的 SSO 登录。请同时将其移出工作区（会退出其登录并阻止再次自动开通），并撤销其创建的 API 密钥和智能体授权：通过 SSO 会话创建的 API 密钥在被撤销前会一直有效。</p>
    <h3>安全说明</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>使用带 PKCE（S256）的授权码流程；一次性的 <code>state</code> 只以哈希形式保存，并通过 Cookie 绑定到发起登录的浏览器；使用 <code>nonce</code>；10 分钟有效；重定向 URI 固定为本服务器的地址。</li>
      <li>id_token 使用提供商的 JWKS 验证（遇到未知的密钥 ID 时重新获取，以支持密钥轮换，最多每 30 秒一次）；检查 <code>iss</code>、<code>aud</code>、<code>azp</code>、<code>exp</code>、<code>nbf</code> 和 <code>iat</code>，允许 60 秒时钟偏差，签发超过 10 分钟的令牌会被拒绝。</li>
      <li>发现文档、JWKS 和令牌请求只发往公网地址，不跟随重定向，并限制为 8 秒和 64 KiB。若提供商位于内网，或测试时使用 http，请设置 <code>SSO_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IDP=true</code>（与 <code>ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS</code> 相互独立）。即使如此，链路本地和云元数据地址（169.254.0.0/16、fe80::/10、fd00:ec2::254、100.100.100.200）、组播地址和 0.0.0.0/8 仍会被拒绝，连接仍固定到已检查的地址，时间、大小和禁止重定向的限制也照样生效。</li>
      <li>连接只会把用户登录到它自己的工作区。将某人移出工作区是最终的：SSO 不会把他重新加回（请同时在身份提供商处移除）。</li>
      <li>退出登录会结束 Montral 会话，但不会退出身份提供商。</li>
      <li>所有者可以在<a href="/docs/api#audit">审计日志</a>中看到所有配置变更、每次 SSO 登录以及被拒绝的登录。</li>
      <li>不支持 SAML，原因见 <code>docs/evidence/2026-11-10-oidc-sso.md</code>。</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="apns-zh">iOS 推送通知（APNs）</h2>
    <p>Montral iOS 应用可以通过推送接收告警。服务器经由 Apple 的 APNs 发送，因此需要 APNs 凭证。以下四个变量全部设置后才会启用推送；此时 <code>GET /api/config</code> 会返回 <code>push.apns: true</code>，告警页里也会出现 <em>手机 App 推送</em> 渠道类型。</p>
    <h3>你需要准备</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>一个 Apple Developer 账号，以及为应用创建的 App ID（开启 Push Notifications 能力）。</li>
      <li>在 <strong>Certificates, Identifiers &amp; Profiles → Keys</strong> 中创建的 APNs Auth Key（<code>.p8</code> 文件）及其 <strong>Key ID</strong>。</li>
      <li>你的 <strong>Team ID</strong> 和应用的 <strong>bundle id</strong>。</li>
    </ul>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>变量</th><th>取值</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>APNS_KEY</code></td><td><code>.p8</code> 文件的内容。可以用字面的 <code>\n</code> 代替换行，写在 <code>.env</code> 里更方便。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>APNS_KEY_ID</code></td><td>密钥的 10 位 id。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>APNS_TEAM_ID</code></td><td>Apple Developer 团队 id。</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>APNS_BUNDLE_ID</code></td><td>应用的 bundle id，用作 APNs topic。</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Docker</strong>：把四个变量写进 <code>.env</code>，然后执行 <code>docker compose up -d</code>。</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>：在 <code>apps/api</code> 中执行 <code>pnpm exec wrangler secret put APNS_KEY</code>（粘贴整个文件），再对 <code>APNS_KEY_ID</code>、<code>APNS_TEAM_ID</code>、<code>APNS_BUNDLE_ID</code> 做同样操作，然后重新部署 API Worker。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>工作方式</h3>
    <p>成员在应用里注册自己的手机；<code>push</code> 渠道会通知工作区中所有已注册设备的成员，并按各自的语言显示。所有者或管理员注册手机时，如果工作区还没有该渠道，会自动创建名为 <em>Mobile app</em> 的渠道。Apple 反馈已失效的手机会被自动清除。</p>
    <p><strong>重要：</strong>APNs 密钥绑定你的 Apple 团队和应用的 bundle id，手机令牌也只对产生它的应用有效。因此官方 Montral 应用只能接收托管服务发出的推送。自托管服务器上，推送适用于你自己用自己的 bundle id 和密钥构建并签名的应用。让官方应用接收自托管服务器推送的中继服务尚未实现。</p>
    <h2 id="custom-domains-zh">状态页自定义域名</h2>
    <p>Docker（Node）服务器可以在独立的主机名（如 <code>status.example.com</code>）上提供状态页。<strong>Cloudflare Workers 部署不支持自定义域名</strong>：在那里设置时 API 会拒绝（<code>400</code>，code 为 <code>custom_domain_unsupported</code>）。</p>
    <p>Montral 不签发证书。由你的反向代理为该域名终止 TLS，并携带原始 <code>Host</code> 头把请求转发给 Montral。</p>
    <h3>1. 认领并验证域名</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>在状态页编辑器中打开<strong>自定义域名</strong>，填写主机名并保存。仅所有者和管理员可以操作。</li>
      <li>按显示内容创建 TXT 记录：名称 <code>_montral-challenge.status.example.com</code>，值 <code>montral-verify=…</code>，必须完全一致。</li>
      <li>点击<strong>验证</strong>。Montral 从服务器查询该记录，要求完全匹配。再次保存域名（即使名称相同）会生成新的值，需要重新验证。</li>
      <li>域名归属由 DNS 决定。任何页面都可以填写某个域名，但只有已发布其 TXT 记录的页面才持有它，且同一时间只有一个页面持有。域名易主时，新所有者发布自己的记录并验证：域名转移到其页面，原页面失去该域名，无需原页面配合。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>2. 把域名指向你的代理</h3>
    <p>为该主机名添加指向代理的 <code>A</code>/<code>AAAA</code> 或 <code>CNAME</code> 记录，然后在代理中添加站点。Caddy 会自动申请证书，并默认保留 <code>Host</code> 头：</p>
    <pre><code is:raw># Caddyfile
app.example.com {
	reverse_proxy montral:8080
}
status.example.com {
	reverse_proxy montral:8080
}</code></pre>
    <p>使用 nginx 时请保留主机名：<code>proxy_set_header Host $host;</code>。如果代理改写了 <code>Host</code>，Montral 会改读 <code>X-Forwarded-Host</code>，但只信任受信代理发来的值（<code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code>，且代理地址在 <code>TRUST_PROXY_PEER_IPS</code> 中）；其他来源的该头会被忽略。</p>
    <h3>域名上提供的内容</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><code>/</code> 是状态页；<code>/rss.xml</code>、<code>/maintenance.ics</code>、<code>/badge.svg</code> 和 <code>/llms.txt</code> 是它的订阅源；页面自身发起的 <code>/api/public/status/&lt;slug&gt;/…</code> 请求照常可用。</li>
      <li>到达服务器、但既不是应用自身地址也不是已验证状态域名的主机名，所有路径都返回 <code>404</code>：在验证之前、或在页面或域名被移除之后指向服务器的域名，永远不会显示应用或其登录页。IP 地址、<code>localhost</code> 和单标签名称（如 compose 服务名）仍可访问应用。</li>
      <li>在已验证的域名上，其他路径一律返回 <code>404</code>：应用、登录和注册、私有 API、Webhook 接收地址、文档以及其他状态页。该域名永远不会提供已登录的应用，也不会读取登录 Cookie。</li>
      <li>公开页面照常可用。密码页面显示密码表单，解锁后只为该域名设置访问 Cookie。仅成员可见的页面在自定义域名上返回 <code>404</code>，因为登录只在主地址进行。分享链接仍指向主地址。</li>
      <li>通过 API 所做的修改会在处理该请求的服务器上立即生效；多台服务器时，其他服务器会在 60 秒内同步。</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>保留 TXT 记录</h3>
    <p>已验证的域名需要持续证明控制权。服务器大约每 6 小时重新查询一次 TXT 记录，查询失败后改为大约每 30 分钟一次（优先检查失败的域名）。短暂的 DNS 问题不会让页面下线：失败记录刚开始时，域名继续提供页面，编辑器会显示失败开始的时间和原因。</p>
    <ul>
      <li>如果记录<strong>缺失或内容不符</strong>已持续 24 小时、且至少检查了三次，验证将被撤销，该域名返回 <code>404</code>。</li>
      <li>如果该域名的 <strong>DNS 完全无法访问</strong>（超时、SERVFAIL、名称服务器失效），页面会继续提供 7 天，之后撤销验证。失败类型在 DNS 无法访问与记录缺失之间切换时，重新开始计算。</li>
      <li>编辑器会显示撤销原因。恢复记录后点击<strong>验证</strong>即可重新在该域名上提供页面。</li>
      <li>域名连续第二次复查失败时（每个失败周期只发一次），以及验证被撤销时（每次撤销只发一次），工作区的所有者和管理员会收到一封邮件（使用各自的语言），普通成员不会收到。这些邮件需要配置 SMTP，并会出现在告警记录中；邮件服务器拒收时会再重试两次，撤销本身从不等待邮件。</li>
      <li>多台服务器共同承担复查：每个域名在数据库中被认领，因此每轮只查询一次。撤销在执行它的服务器上立即生效，其他服务器在 60 秒内同步。</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="oncall-zh">值班表与升级</h2>
    <p>侧边栏工作区部分的<strong>值班</strong>页面用于管理值班表、替班和升级策略。服务器无需额外配置，只依赖告警已在使用的设置：被通知的人会收到发往其账号邮箱的邮件（需配置邮件发送），以及发往其注册手机的推送（需配置 <a href="#apns-zh">APNs</a>）。</p>
    <h3>值班表</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>值班表有一个 IANA 时区和一个或多个<strong>层级</strong>。每个层级按每天、每周（指定星期几）或每 N 小时在成员之间轮换，从开始日期起在当地时间交接。层级可以限定在某些时段内生效，例如工作日 09:00-17:00。</li>
      <li>在后面的层级有人值班的时段，它会覆盖前面的层级；不在其时段内时，由前面的层级补上。</li>
      <li>短于 24 小时的轮值按从第一次交接起经过的实际时间计算，因此夏令时切换时每个班次都保持完整时长（1 小时轮值在春季切换当晚不会少掉任何人的一小时）。每天、每周及更长的轮值按当地墙钟时间进行。</li>
      <li>交接按当地时间进行，夏令时切换时也是如此：如果交接时间在春季切换时被跳过（例如纽约的 02:30），则在时钟跳变时交接；秋季切换时重复出现的时间只使用一次，即第一次出现时。30 分钟的切换（豪勋爵岛）同样适用。</li>
      <li><strong>替班</strong>让某人在一段时间内值班，优先于所有层级；替班重叠时以最新创建的为准。</li>
      <li>离开工作区的人会被跳过：其轮次交给层级中的下一个人，其替班也不再生效。如需彻底移除，请编辑该层级。</li>
      <li>每个人都可以通过私密 iCalendar 链接订阅自己的班次（过去一周和未来 60 天），并可随时更换或关闭该链接。</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>权限</h3>
    <p>所有者和管理员可以创建和修改值班表、层级、策略以及任何人的替班。成员可以查看全部内容（包括当前值班人），可以为自己添加替班（顶班或换班），也可以删除自己为自己添加的替班。每次更改都会记入审计日志。两个人同时保存同一个值班表时不会互相覆盖：后保存的会因冲突被拒绝，并提示内容已被修改。</p>
    <h3>升级</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>升级策略</strong>由若干步骤组成。每一步通知渠道、指定的人员以及其值班表上的值班人，然后等待超时时间内有人确认，否则进入下一步。最后一步之后可以从头重复几次，然后停止。</li>
      <li>在监控设置中为监控选择策略。事件一开启就会通知第一步（调度器每分钟运行一次）。未选择策略的监控继续使用告警页面中项目的升级级别，这些级别现在也可以通知值班表。</li>
      <li>确认事件即停止升级（包括即将发出的通知）；若事件还没有负责人，确认者会成为负责人（此前确认总会重新指派事件）。解决事件则全部停止。</li>
      <li>策略的第一步不会再次通知已收到该事件故障告警的渠道。删除策略后，其未结束事件停止升级；其监控的新事件使用项目的升级级别。</li>
      <li>每个值班表最多保留 500 个未结束的替班（每人 50 个），每个最长 90 天，最多提前一年开始。日历链接只能在登录状态下创建，更换时会提示旧链接已失效。</li>
      <li>即使有多台服务器，每一步也只发送一次，并会写入事件时间线（仅团队可见）和审计日志。发送失败的邮件和推送会像其他告警一样重试，并显示在告警日志中。</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="after-zh">安装之后</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>创建第一个监控项，再创建<a href="/docs/embed">状态页</a>，需要的话把状态嵌入到你的网站。</li>
      <li>通过 <a href="/docs/api">API</a> 自动化，或用 <a href="/docs/mcp">MCP</a> 接入 Agent，示例里的域名换成你自己的。</li>
    </ul>
